&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fanatics Collectibles is looking for an Inventory Management Associate to support inventory operations for our Autograph Operations team. This role reports into our Inventory Management department and is responsible for ensuring on card autos are accurately accounted for, plus ensuring that our athlete partners are paid in a timely fashion. This role additionally plays a direct part in the finalization and packout of products for Fanatics Collectibles. Candidates with a passion for sports, culture, &amp;amp; entertainment will find themselves a strong cultural fit.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conducts analysis of primarily on card autographs post-quality control before data entry into Cards-in Reporting base&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Complete program audits and packout of live cards for programs, including shipping pallets to external packout vendors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Guide check-in process of programs in collation with the assistance of the manufacturing team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Completes transactions in Oracle ERP to receive autographs into inventory and perform subinventory transfers to assign cards to programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the warehouse space including physical organization of cards on shelves&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Perform final QC check for Auto Ops across all licenses and programs to ensure high quality autograph cards are being sent to collectors&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate needed adjustments or program-level updates to internal and external stakeholders as programs complete packout&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Ideal Candidate:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Dallas / Sunnyvale, TX based&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelors Degree in Business, Analytics, Finance or a relatable field, preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;0-3 years’ experience in warehouse or production environments, specifically related to inventory management or quality control&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong critical thinking, analytical, and problem-solving capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient experience with Oracle or equivalent ERP&#39;s, strongly preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience with data visualization tools such as Power BI, Tableau, or Excel, required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working in a fast-paced environment and able to sit and focus on a computer screen for extended periods of time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
