&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 class=&quot;job-details__description-header text-color-secondary font-family-secondary&quot; data-bind=&quot;i18n: &#39;job-details.employer-description-title&#39;&quot;&gt;About Us&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;job-details__description-content basic-formatter&quot; data-bind=&quot;html: pageData().job.corporateDescription&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Fanatics is building a leading global digital sports platform. We ignite the passions of global sports fans and maximize the presence and reach for our hundreds of sports partners globally by offering products and services across Fanatics Commerce, Fanatics Collectibles, and Fanatics Betting &amp;amp; Gaming, allowing sports fans to Buy, Collect, and Bet. Through the Fanatics platform, sports fans can buy licensed fan gear, jerseys, lifestyle and streetwear products, headwear, and hardgoods; collect physical and digital trading cards, sports memorabilia, and other digital assets; and bet as the company builds its Sportsbook and iGaming platform. Fanatics has an established database of over 100 million global sports fans; a global partner network with approximately 900 sports properties, including major national and international professional sports leagues, players associations, teams, colleges, college conferences and retail partners, 2,500 athletes and celebrities, and 200 exclusive athletes; and over 2,000 retail locations, including its Lids retail stores. Our more than 22,000 employees are committed to relentlessly enhancing the fan experience and delighting sports fans globally.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Company&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Fanatics Collectibles is a new company operating at the intersection of collectibles, culture, and technology. Backed by world-class investors, operators, and sports &amp;amp; entertainment partners, we are building the global leader in next-generation collectibles. As part of the broader Fanatics ecosystem, we leverage a digital sports platform that spans over 900 sports properties and engages more than 81 million fans. Together, we are reimagining every part of the collectibles experience for fans, partners, and creators.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Fanatics Collectibles is seeking a Director of Project Management to lead day-to-day execution, with a focus on our Entertainment portfolio. With additional licenses expected to come online, this leader will help scale how licensed trading-card products are developed and brought to market.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;The Director will lead an existing team of project management professionals while building the processes, operating rhythms, and cross-functional alignment needed to support a growing portfolio. This is a builder-operator role requiring someone who can resolve immediate execution challenges while creating a more predictable and scalable project management function.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;The ideal candidate has led teams in licensed physical products, consumer products, entertainment merchandise, or a similarly complex product-development environment. They are comfortable navigating external licensor requirements, shifting dependencies, and high-visibility launches.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will be doing...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead and develop the Entertainment project management team:&lt;/strong&gt; Set priorities, clarify ownership, coach team members, and create a culture of accountability, collaboration, and continuous improvement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive portfolio execution:&lt;/strong&gt; Oversee the end-to-end development and launch of multiple licensed trading-card properties, ensuring dependencies, milestones, risks, and decisions remain visible and actively managed.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Resolve complex execution challenges:&lt;/strong&gt; Serve as a senior escalation point for product-development and launch issues, bringing together internal teams and external partners to reach timely solutions.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build scalable operations:&lt;/strong&gt; Improve project management processes, tools, reporting, and communication practices to support portfolio growth and make execution more consistent and predictable.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Manage cross-functional and licensor alignment:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner closely with product teams, executives, and external licensors, including partners who may be unfamiliar with trading-card development.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strengthen risk management:&lt;/strong&gt; Anticipate potential issues, develop mitigation plans, and communicate portfolio risks and tradeoffs clearly to senior leadership.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will bring...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;10+ years progressive experience leading complex project or program management within licensed physical products, consumer products, entertainment merchandise, or a related environment.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Demonstrated experience managing and developing project management professionals.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Track record of improving processes while maintaining accountability for active, fast-moving work.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Experience navigating external licensors, intellectual-property requirements, or other dependencies outside the organization’s direct control.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Strong executive communication, negotiation, and stakeholder-management skills.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Ability to bring structure and clarity to evolving, ambiguous, or high-pressure environments.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Experience with project tracking, forecasting, and portfolio-reporting tools; direct experience with Workfront or Airtable is helpful but not required.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Interest in sports, entertainment, trading cards, or collectibles is a plus.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s1&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Ensure your Fanatics job offer is legitimate and don’t fall victim to fraud.&amp;nbsp; Fanatics never seeks payment from job applicants. Feel free to ask your recruiter for a phone call or other type of communication for interview, and ensure your communication is coming from a Fanatics email address (including @collectfanatics.com).&amp;nbsp; For added security, where possible, apply through our company website at&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.fanaticsinc.com/careers&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s2&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;www.fanaticsinc.com/careers&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The salary range represents base pay only and does not include short-term or long-term incentive compensation. &amp;nbsp;This salary range is specific to Los Angeles and may not be applicable to other locations. &amp;nbsp;When determining base pay, as part of a final compensation package, we consider several factors such as location, experience, qualifications, and training. For information about our benefits, please visit&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://benefitsatfanatics.com/&quot;&gt;https://benefitsatfanatics.com/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Los Angeles Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$173,650&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$184,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By submitting your application, you agree to our terms of service and acknowledge you have read our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://static1.squarespace.com/static/5ff494b9931735466ce28d5b/t/69de53bde2c02c25e9c38758/1776178110037/Candidate+Privacy+Policy+April+2026.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Candidate Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Fanatics will never ask candidates for money, banking information, or other sensitive personal information as part of the interview process. If you receive a suspicious message claiming to be from Fanatics recruiting, please do not respond and report it&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:recruiting-fraud@fanaticsinc.com&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;here&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 class=&quot;job-details__description-header text-color-secondary font-family-secondary&quot; data-bind=&quot;i18n: &#39;job-details.employer-description-title&#39;&quot;&gt;About Us&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;job-details__description-content basic-formatter&quot; data-bind=&quot;html: pageData().job.corporateDescription&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Fanatics is building a leading global digital sports platform. We ignite the passions of global sports fans and maximize the presence and reach for our hundreds of sports partners globally by offering products and services across Fanatics Commerce, Fanatics Collectibles, and Fanatics Betting &amp;amp; Gaming, allowing sports fans to Buy, Collect, and Bet. Through the Fanatics platform, sports fans can buy licensed fan gear, jerseys, lifestyle and streetwear products, headwear, and hardgoods; collect physical and digital trading cards, sports memorabilia, and other digital assets; and bet as the company builds its Sportsbook and iGaming platform. Fanatics has an established database of over 100 million global sports fans; a global partner network with approximately 900 sports properties, including major national and international professional sports leagues, players associations, teams, colleges, college conferences and retail partners, 2,500 athletes and celebrities, and 200 exclusive athletes; and over 2,000 retail locations, including its Lids retail stores. Our more than 22,000 employees are committed to relentlessly enhancing the fan experience and delighting sports fans globally.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Company&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Fanatics Collectibles is a new company operating at the intersection of collectibles, culture, and technology. Backed by world-class investors, operators, and sports &amp;amp; entertainment partners, we are building the global leader in next-generation collectibles. As part of the broader Fanatics ecosystem, we leverage a digital sports platform that spans over 900 sports properties and engages more than 81 million fans. Together, we are reimagining every part of the collectibles experience for fans, partners, and creators.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Fanatics Collectibles is seeking a Director of Project Management to lead day-to-day execution, with a focus on our Entertainment portfolio. With additional licenses expected to come online, this leader will help scale how licensed trading-card products are developed and brought to market.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;The Director will lead an existing team of project management professionals while building the processes, operating rhythms, and cross-functional alignment needed to support a growing portfolio. This is a builder-operator role requiring someone who can resolve immediate execution challenges while creating a more predictable and scalable project management function.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;The ideal candidate has led teams in licensed physical products, consumer products, entertainment merchandise, or a similarly complex product-development environment. They are comfortable navigating external licensor requirements, shifting dependencies, and high-visibility launches.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will be doing...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lead and develop the Entertainment project management team:&lt;/strong&gt; Set priorities, clarify ownership, coach team members, and create a culture of accountability, collaboration, and continuous improvement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Drive portfolio execution:&lt;/strong&gt; Oversee the end-to-end development and launch of multiple licensed trading-card properties, ensuring dependencies, milestones, risks, and decisions remain visible and actively managed.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Resolve complex execution challenges:&lt;/strong&gt; Serve as a senior escalation point for product-development and launch issues, bringing together internal teams and external partners to reach timely solutions.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build scalable operations:&lt;/strong&gt; Improve project management processes, tools, reporting, and communication practices to support portfolio growth and make execution more consistent and predictable.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Manage cross-functional and licensor alignment:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner closely with product teams, executives, and external licensors, including partners who may be unfamiliar with trading-card development.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Strengthen risk management:&lt;/strong&gt; Anticipate potential issues, develop mitigation plans, and communicate portfolio risks and tradeoffs clearly to senior leadership.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will bring...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;10+ years progressive experience leading complex project or program management within licensed physical products, consumer products, entertainment merchandise, or a related environment.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Demonstrated experience managing and developing project management professionals.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Track record of improving processes while maintaining accountability for active, fast-moving work.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Experience navigating external licensors, intellectual-property requirements, or other dependencies outside the organization’s direct control.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Strong executive communication, negotiation, and stakeholder-management skills.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Ability to bring structure and clarity to evolving, ambiguous, or high-pressure environments.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Experience with project tracking, forecasting, and portfolio-reporting tools; direct experience with Workfront or Airtable is helpful but not required.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Interest in sports, entertainment, trading cards, or collectibles is a plus.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s1&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Ensure your Fanatics job offer is legitimate and don’t fall victim to fraud.&amp;nbsp; Fanatics never seeks payment from job applicants. Feel free to ask your recruiter for a phone call or other type of communication for interview, and ensure your communication is coming from a Fanatics email address (including @collectfanatics.com).&amp;nbsp; For added security, where possible, apply through our company website at&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.fanaticsinc.com/careers&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s2&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;www.fanaticsinc.com/careers&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By submitting your application, you agree to our terms of service and acknowledge you have read our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://static1.squarespace.com/static/5ff494b9931735466ce28d5b/t/69de53bde2c02c25e9c38758/1776178110037/Candidate+Privacy+Policy+April+2026.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Candidate Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Fanatics will never ask candidates for money, banking information, or other sensitive personal information as part of the interview process. If you receive a suspicious message claiming to be from Fanatics recruiting, please do not respond and report it&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:recruiting-fraud@fanaticsinc.com&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;here&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 class=&quot;job-details__description-header text-color-secondary font-family-secondary&quot; data-bind=&quot;i18n: &#39;job-details.employer-description-title&#39;&quot;&gt;About Us&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;job-details__description-content basic-formatter&quot; data-bind=&quot;html: pageData().job.corporateDescription&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Fanatics is building a leading global digital sports platform. We ignite the passions of global sports fans and maximize the presence and reach for our hundreds of sports partners globally by offering products and services across Fanatics Commerce, Fanatics Collectibles, and Fanatics Betting &amp;amp; Gaming, allowing sports fans to Buy, Collect, and Bet. Through the Fanatics platform, sports fans can buy licensed fan gear, jerseys, lifestyle and streetwear products, headwear, and hardgoods; collect physical and digital trading cards, sports memorabilia, and other digital assets; and bet as the company builds its Sportsbook and iGaming platform. Fanatics has an established database of over 100 million global sports fans; a global partner network with approximately 900 sports properties, including major national and international professional sports leagues, players associations, teams, colleges, college conferences and retail partners, 2,500 athletes and celebrities, and 200 exclusive athletes; and over 2,000 retail locations, including its Lids retail stores. Our more than 22,000 employees are committed to relentlessly enhancing the fan experience and delighting sports fans globally.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Early Careers Talent Community&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who we are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Fanatics Collectibles is the company behind Topps, the trading card brand founded in 1938. We hold exclusive trading card rights with MLB, the NBA, and the NFL, and partner with leagues and entertainment properties around the world, from the Premier League, UEFA, FIFA, and Formula 1 to UFC, WWE, Star Wars, and Marvel. Our products sell in more than 100 countries. We are a product and technology company, spanning physical cards and collectibles, Fanatics Collect, our digital marketplace and live-commerce platform, and a newly formed Trading Card Games studio in Seattle.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The 2027 Internship Program&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;A paid, in-person, 10-week summer program (June 7 – August 13, 2027) across our offices. Interns take part in a speaker series, Hobby 101, cohort events, and a peer-mentor program.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Potential business areas&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Product&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Licensing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Athlete Partnerships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercial / Sales&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Marketing &amp;amp; Social Media&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategy&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Finance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Legal&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;People&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Trading Card Games (TCG)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fanatics Collect (Digital)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who should join&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Students and recent graduates interested in interning or starting a career with us. We prioritize students entering their senior year for internships but welcome all strong candidates. Legal internship opportunities are open to current law students, with a preference for second-year students (2Ls). No collecting background is required; we hire for curiosity, skills, and drive, and we value experience from coursework, clubs, athletics, military service, volunteering, employment, and personal projects.&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What happens next&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Share your resume and tell us your areas of interest and preferred cities. You&#39;ll receive alerts when matching roles post, invitations to our virtual Opportunity Sessions in October and November, and preparation resources ahead of applications opening. Joining the Talent Community does not create an application; you&#39;ll still apply to specific roles when they post.&lt;br&gt;Internships are in office five days a week. Housing and relocation support are not provided. Compensation, eligibility, and location are confirmed on each official posting.&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By submitting your application, you agree to our terms of service and acknowledge you have read our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://static1.squarespace.com/static/5ff494b9931735466ce28d5b/t/69de53bde2c02c25e9c38758/1776178110037/Candidate+Privacy+Policy+April+2026.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Candidate Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Fanatics will never ask candidates for money, banking information, or other sensitive personal information as part of the interview process. If you receive a suspicious message claiming to be from Fanatics recruiting, please do not respond and report it&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:recruiting-fraud@fanaticsinc.com&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;here&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 class=&quot;job-details__description-header text-color-secondary font-family-secondary&quot; data-bind=&quot;i18n: &#39;job-details.employer-description-title&#39;&quot;&gt;About Us&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;job-details__description-content basic-formatter&quot; data-bind=&quot;html: pageData().job.corporateDescription&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Fanatics is building a leading global digital sports platform. We ignite the passions of global sports fans and maximize the presence and reach for our hundreds of sports partners globally by offering products and services across Fanatics Commerce, Fanatics Collectibles, and Fanatics Betting &amp;amp; Gaming, allowing sports fans to Buy, Collect, and Bet. Through the Fanatics platform, sports fans can buy licensed fan gear, jerseys, lifestyle and streetwear products, headwear, and hardgoods; collect physical and digital trading cards, sports memorabilia, and other digital assets; and bet as the company builds its Sportsbook and iGaming platform. Fanatics has an established database of over 100 million global sports fans; a global partner network with approximately 900 sports properties, including major national and international professional sports leagues, players associations, teams, colleges, college conferences and retail partners, 2,500 athletes and celebrities, and 200 exclusive athletes; and over 2,000 retail locations, including its Lids retail stores. Our more than 22,000 employees are committed to relentlessly enhancing the fan experience and delighting sports fans globally.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;We are seeking an experienced and results-driven Ecommerce Assistant Manager to join the Ecommerce Commercial Team. The Ecommerce Commercial Team is responsible for driving growth across Fanatics Collectibles’ digital channels through strong commercial planning, operational execution, reporting, and cross-functional coordination. This role will own the day-to-day management of our third-party (3P) marketplace business across Amazon U.S. and Walmart.com, as well as the operational launch and scaling of our Target DSV program.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;This role carries broad ownership across the domestic marketplace business, including performance management and reporting, launch and item setup management, content and site merchandising, fulfillment (FBA/WFS) and inventory management, advertising execution and optimization, and agency and partner management—along with operational leadership of Target DSV.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;isSelectedEnd&quot;&gt;The ideal candidate is a proactive self-starter who can operate independently, make sound decisions within an established channel strategy, and raise the bar for execution quality across the business. This role will report to the Ecommerce Manager, Marketplaces and work closely with the Go-to-Market (GTM), Ecommerce Operations, Analytics, Finance, Customer Service, Creative, Legal &amp;amp; Licensing, and Logistics teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;What you will be doing...&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;3P Marketplace Channel Management (Amazon U.S. &amp;amp; Walmart)&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and run the daily and weekly operating cadence for Amazon U.S. and Walmart.com, managing sales, traffic, conversion, Buy Box health, inventory position, and sell-through against allocation plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own pre-order setup and go-live timing, making in-flight adjustments to capture demand ahead of street dates and reduce revenue cliffs between releases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage listing health, pricing, and channel policy compliance, including Final Sale, and drive Seller Central and Walmart Seller Center escalations through resolution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify competitive and reseller threats to Buy Box performance, pricing, and sales velocity, and drive corrective action plans to protect performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Launch Management &amp;amp; Item Setup&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own end-to-end item setup and launch management in Amazon Seller Central and Walmart Seller Center, driving each SKU through the full setup-to-street timeline across operations, content, and advertising workstreams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and continuously improve the launch playbook across pre-order, street date, and post-launch stages to raise readiness standards and eliminate execution issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead cross-functional launch readiness with GTM, Creative, Logistics, and Operations, holding workstream owners accountable for content, inventory, and advertising milestones.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage launch sequencing across concurrent SKUs and channels to stabilize weekly revenue and keep multiple listings live at all times.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Content Management &amp;amp; Site Merchandising&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the quality and performance of Amazon and Walmart product detail pages, including titles, bullets, descriptions, imagery, A+ content, attributes, and taxonomy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gather product assets and manage revision cycles with our external content agency, Marketing, and Product teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own merchandising for the Amazon and Walmart Brand Stores, keeping new releases, categories, and product tiles current with the live assortment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive regular listing audits and content optimizations to keep product pages accurate, compliant, and aligned with brand and licensing requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Fulfillment (FBA/WFS) &amp;amp; Inventory Management&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee FBA and WFS shipments, partnering with Logistics and warehouse teams on labeling, preparation, palletization, bills of lading, and carrier pickups.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage inbound flow and fulfillment center check-in, escalating and resolving receiving delays that put street dates or Prime and two-day delivery availability at risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own receiving reconciliation and reimbursement claims for lost or misrouted inventory, protecting revenue and margin.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own inventory health and replenishment planning to keep top sellers in stock throughout their full demand window.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Advertising Execution &amp;amp; Optimization&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the day-to-day execution and in-flight optimization of the phased advertising strategy across Amazon Sponsored Products, Sponsored Brands, and Sponsored Display, as well as Walmart Connect.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make scale, trim, and cut decisions within established ROAS and TACoS guardrails, and recommend strategic adjustments based on campaign performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own weekly advertising reporting and budget pacing across the launch calendar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Target DSV Launch &amp;amp; Operations&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the operational lead for the Target DSV program, driving end-to-end launch readiness across item setup, content requirements, data and feed validation, and operational testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Ecommerce Operations, Logistics, and Technology teams to establish and manage DSV order flow, inventory alignment, and fulfillment requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own fulfillment SLA performance, service issue resolution, and launch-blocker escalation to keep the program on schedule.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the process documentation, trackers, and playbooks needed to scale the DSV model across additional assortment over time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Forecasting, Reporting &amp;amp; Commercial Analysis&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own weekly and monthly business reporting across Amazon U.S., Walmart.com, and Target DSV, including sales, units, traffic, conversion, inventory status, returns, and advertising performance, and deliver the insights behind the numbers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and own SKU-level sell-through and forecasting models using historical benchmarks, early sales reads, and launch assumptions to inform allocation planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own progress tracking against sales, unit, and inventory goals, proactively surfacing risks, gaps, and upside opportunities with recommended actions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver leadership-ready recaps, post-launch analyses, and commercial planning materials that shape decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;Cross-Functional Leadership &amp;amp; Analytics Enablement&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive 3P marketplace and Target DSV initiatives across functions, owning timelines, accountability, and next steps through completion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Represent the channels in internal meetings, presenting performance, priorities, and recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Analytics and Data teams to evolve dashboards and reporting from manual pulls to automated pipelines, owning data validation and business requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Anticipate blockers, create visibility into risks and dependencies, and drive decisions that keep priorities moving.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will bring...&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3–5 years of experience in ecommerce, marketplace management, merchandising, digital operations, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience managing Amazon Seller Central and/or Walmart Seller Center, including item setup, FBA/WFS shipment creation, listing management, and case management, is required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong proficiency in Excel and/or Google Sheets, with the ability to build, maintain, and analyze large datasets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning product content, merchandising, and item setup across ecommerce or marketplace environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing external agencies, vendors, or marketplace partner relationships.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with DSV, dropship, or first-party retail partner operations, such as Target, is preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to independently manage multiple workstreams in a fast-paced environment and drive them to completion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical mindset, with the ability to turn data into clear insights and recommended actions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working and leading cross-functionally with Operations, Analytics, Merchandising, Marketing, Finance, and Creative teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong verbal and written communication skills, with the ability to present findings and recommendations to leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong proficiency in AI prompting, with the ability to automate manual tasks and improve team efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with reporting or visualization tools such as Sigma, Snowflake, Power BI, or similar platforms is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for sports, collectibles, and/or ecommerce is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
