&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 class=&quot;job-details__description-header text-color-secondary font-family-secondary&quot; data-bind=&quot;i18n: &#39;job-details.employer-description-title&#39;&quot;&gt;About Us&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;job-details__description-content basic-formatter&quot; data-bind=&quot;html: pageData().job.corporateDescription&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Fanatics is building a leading global digital sports platform. We ignite the passions of global sports fans and maximize the presence and reach for our hundreds of sports partners globally by offering products and services across Fanatics Commerce, Fanatics Collectibles, and Fanatics Betting &amp;amp; Gaming, allowing sports fans to Buy, Collect, and Bet. Through the Fanatics platform, sports fans can buy licensed fan gear, jerseys, lifestyle and streetwear products, headwear, and hardgoods; collect physical and digital trading cards, sports memorabilia, and other digital assets; and bet as the company builds its Sportsbook and iGaming platform. Fanatics has an established database of over 100 million global sports fans; a global partner network with approximately 900 sports properties, including major national and international professional sports leagues, players associations, teams, colleges, college conferences and retail partners, 2,500 athletes and celebrities, and 200 exclusive athletes; and over 2,000 retail locations, including its Lids retail stores. Our more than 22,000 employees are committed to relentlessly enhancing the fan experience and delighting sports fans globally.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Help shape the future of Topps.com&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Topps has defined the trading card hobby for generations. Now, we’re reimagining how that legacy comes to life digitally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We’re looking for a Lead Product &amp;amp; Brand Designer to help transform Topps.com from a traditional e-commerce site into a destination for collectors, one that brings products to life through storytelling, content, interaction, and exceptional design.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hybrid product and visual design role. You’ll work across user journeys, commerce experiences, design systems, and brand expression to make Topps.com more intuitive, engaging, and unmistakably Topps. You’ll partner closely with Product, Engineering, Brand, and Content teams to turn functional experiences into memorable ones.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You should be equally comfortable improving a user flow, designing a product page, building a scalable visual system, and exploring how motion or interaction can make an experience more compelling.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A note on portfolios&lt;/strong&gt;: We want to see strong product and UX work, flows, systems, interfaces, and shipped digital experiences, alongside exceptional visual craft. Portfolios focused entirely on campaigns, identity, or marketing assets without product or UI examples will not be a fit.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product Experience &amp;amp; Commerce&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and evolve key experiences across Topps.com, from discovery and product education to purchase and post-purchase&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product and Engineering to improve usability, information architecture, hierarchy, and interaction patterns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reimagine product pages as collector destinations, even when a product is sold out&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Balance storytelling and visual expression with clarity, accessibility, conversion, and performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prototype new concepts and help teams move from ideas to polished, shippable experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Digital Storytelling&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bring Topps products, athletes, sets, and stories to life through immersive digital experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Explore how editorial content, collecting history, product details, and the broader Fanatics ecosystem can enrich the shopping journey&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create experiences that build anticipation around launches and give collectors reasons to return&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate complex product information into clear, compelling stories&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Interaction, Motion &amp;amp; Craft&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use motion, interaction, and moments of delight to make Topps.com feel more dynamic and distinctive&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define where expressive design adds value—and where the experience should remain simple and focused&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Push the quality of the work from early concept through final implementation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with Engineering to preserve design intent in the shipped experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Brand &amp;amp; Design Systems&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate the Topps brand into scalable patterns for digital product experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evolve visual systems across typography, color, layout, imagery, components, and motion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to a cohesive system that can support different sports, products, audiences, and launches&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create guidelines that help internal teams and external partners apply the experience consistently&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaboration &amp;amp; Leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work across Product, Engineering, Brand, Content, Marketing, and Commerce teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide creative direction and constructive feedback throughout the design process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor other designers and help raise the standard of craft across the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities, build alignment, and move work forward with limited oversight&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who You Are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8–10+ years of design experience with demonstrated product or UX design work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A hybrid designer who combines strong product thinking with exceptional visual craft&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable moving from user flows and information architecture to detailed UI and interaction design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experienced designing responsive web and e-commerce experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A systems thinker who can create distinctive experiences that scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Skilled at translating brand strategy into functional product design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable partnering closely with Product Managers and Engineers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong in both concept and execution, from early prototypes to pixel-level polish&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experienced using storytelling, motion, and interaction to improve digital experiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A proactive, hands-on designer who finds opportunities and pushes the work forward&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passionate about the hobby, or excited to become deeply immersed in it&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Join Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Topps has shaped collecting culture for more than 70 years. Backed by Fanatics and exclusive licensing relationships across MLB, the NFL, and the NBA, we have a unique opportunity to reinvent how collectors discover, experience, and purchase the products they love.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The experiences you design will help define the next chapter of one of the most iconic brands in sports and collecting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What That Means on the Design Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We move fast.&lt;/strong&gt; There’s a lot to build, and we work with urgency while protecting the quality of the experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We design for collectors&lt;/strong&gt;. Every decision should create greater clarity, excitement, or value for the people using the product.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We think beyond transactions&lt;/strong&gt;. Topps.com should be a destination for discovery, storytelling, and collecting—not simply a place to check out.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We design for scale&lt;/strong&gt;. Our systems must flex across sports, products, markets, and collector journeys while remaining unmistakably Topps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’re pragmatic&lt;/strong&gt;. We pursue ambitious ideas and know how to simplify, prioritize, and ship.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’re hands-on&lt;/strong&gt;. We lead through the work, from prototyping and testing to interaction details and final polish.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is an opportunity to help transform Topps.com into the digital home the hobby deserves, connecting an iconic brand’s history with the future of collecting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s1&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Ensure your Fanatics job offer is legitimate and don’t fall victim to fraud.&amp;nbsp; Fanatics never seeks payment from job applicants.&amp;nbsp;Feel free to ask your recruiter for a phone call or other type of communication for interview, and ensure your communication is coming from a Fanatics email address (including @collectfanatics.com).&amp;nbsp; For added security, where possible, apply through our company website at&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.fanaticsinc.com/careers&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s2&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;www.fanaticsinc.com/careers&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The salary range represents base pay only and does not include short-term or long-term incentive compensation. &amp;nbsp;This salary range is specific to Los Angeles and may not be applicable to other locations. &amp;nbsp;When determining base pay, as part of a final compensation package, we consider several factors such as location, experience, qualifications, and training. For information about our benefits, please visit&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://benefitsatfanatics.com/&quot;&gt;https://benefitsatfanatics.com/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Los Angeles Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$140,120&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$175,150 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By submitting your application, you agree to our terms of service and acknowledge you have read our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://static1.squarespace.com/static/5ff494b9931735466ce28d5b/t/69de53bde2c02c25e9c38758/1776178110037/Candidate+Privacy+Policy+April+2026.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Candidate Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Fanatics will never ask candidates for money, banking information, or other sensitive personal information as part of the interview process. If you receive a suspicious message claiming to be from Fanatics recruiting, please do not respond and report it&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:recruiting-fraud@fanaticsinc.com&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;here&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 class=&quot;job-details__description-header text-color-secondary font-family-secondary&quot; data-bind=&quot;i18n: &#39;job-details.employer-description-title&#39;&quot;&gt;About Us&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;job-details__description-content basic-formatter&quot; data-bind=&quot;html: pageData().job.corporateDescription&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Fanatics is building a leading global digital sports platform. We ignite the passions of global sports fans and maximize the presence and reach for our hundreds of sports partners globally by offering products and services across Fanatics Commerce, Fanatics Collectibles, and Fanatics Betting &amp;amp; Gaming, allowing sports fans to Buy, Collect, and Bet. Through the Fanatics platform, sports fans can buy licensed fan gear, jerseys, lifestyle and streetwear products, headwear, and hardgoods; collect physical and digital trading cards, sports memorabilia, and other digital assets; and bet as the company builds its Sportsbook and iGaming platform. Fanatics has an established database of over 100 million global sports fans; a global partner network with approximately 900 sports properties, including major national and international professional sports leagues, players associations, teams, colleges, college conferences and retail partners, 2,500 athletes and celebrities, and 200 exclusive athletes; and over 2,000 retail locations, including its Lids retail stores. Our more than 22,000 employees are committed to relentlessly enhancing the fan experience and delighting sports fans globally.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fanatics Collectibles is the home of sports cards, trading cards, and collectibles for over 100 million fans worldwide. As part of the global Fanatics platform, we&#39;re rebuilding how collectors discover, buy, sell, and experience their hobby with world class technology and product experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As part of Fanatics Collectibles’ continued global growth, we are establishing a new technology hub in Mexico City focused on operational excellence, platform scalability, trust, and customer experience. This team partners closely with Customer Experience (CX), Trust &amp;amp; Safety, Fraud Prevention, Payments, and Financial Operations organizations to build scalable systems and operational tooling that support millions of users and transactions globally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Topps Collector Engagement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Topps is transforming the trading card from a physical product into a connected collector experience. Through scanning, digital claiming, progression programs and partner activations, collectors can authenticate, track, unlock and redeem against the cards they own — bridging the physical product and the digital collector account.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Collector Engagement team builds that technology layer. The team delivers progression and quest experiences, redemption and reward mechanics, leaderboards, retail and live-event check-ins, in-venue collector moments, and the integrations that turn a scanned card into an account-level event. Programs launch against a calendar set by card releases and sports moments, so the team builds reusable platform capability rather than one-off campaign code.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are seeking a Lead Software Engineer to lead a small cohort of engineers building the collector-facing platform behind Topps collector engagement programs while remaining deeply hands-on in the design and delivery of production software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role combines people leadership with senior-level frontend engineering. The Lead will be accountable for the team’s execution, technical quality and development, while personally owning and contributing to complex frontend capabilities, architecture decisions, performance and real-time interaction. Working closely with Product, Design, Backend and Platform Engineering, this role will translate program requirements into shared components, state handling and telemetry that serve many programs rather than one.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a player-coach, this leader will set technical direction, establish priorities, coach and develop engineers, remove delivery blockers and raise engineering standards. The role is expected to spend significant time designing, coding, reviewing and operating production software while ensuring the broader cohort delivers against Collector Engagement priorities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, coach and develop a small cohort of frontend engineers working on Collector Engagement, with accountability for team execution, technical quality and individual growth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set team priorities, allocate work and coordinate execution against Collector Engagement goals, release milestones and program commitments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Remain deeply hands-on: design, develop, test and maintain complex application features and platform components supporting collector engagement programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the technical design and end-to-end delivery of significant frontend features and platform capabilities, contributing directly where technical complexity or delivery risk is highest&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the frontend architecture for program surfaces, including component model, state management, data fetching, and the boundary between shared platform and per-program code&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solve complex and sometimes ambiguous engineering problems involving performance, scalability, reliability, real-time interaction and user experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make sound technical and team execution decisions with appropriate independence, balancing program requirements, engineering quality, scalability, delivery commitments and long-term maintainability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead architecture decisions, technical planning, design reviews and the evolution of frontend engineering patterns across the cohort&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Product, Design, Backend and Platform Engineering to translate program requirements into reusable technical solutions and clear engineering plans&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and evolve API contracts, client workflows and integration patterns, and challenge contracts that push avoidable complexity into the client&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design the shared component and pattern layer with Design so a new program is largely configuration plus a thin custom layer&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish and enforce performance budgets for experiences used mid-event and on low-end devices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the frontend telemetry standard so program analytics are consistent across surfaces&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write clean, maintainable, well-tested code and establish strong patterns and best practices through direct contribution, code review and coaching&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve engineering systems and practices across release management, CI/CD, testing, observability, crash reporting and operational support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively identify technical, delivery and team capacity risks; remove blockers; and escalate or adjust plans when needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead execution for initiatives that may span multiple engineers, systems or partner teams, ensuring ownership, sequencing and follow-through&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide regular coaching, actionable feedback, technical guidance and development support to engineers, and contribute to hiring and team planning as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create an environment of clear expectations, healthy engineering practices and strong collaboration across the Collector Engagement cohort&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with engineering and product leadership on staffing, workload, delivery tradeoffs and execution planning for Collector Engagement priorities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Influence engineering standards and practices within the team and collaborate with adjacent engineering teams on shared technical challenges&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stay current with frontend ecosystem trends, libraries and development patterns and apply relevant advancements to the platform&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of professional frontend or mobile development experience, or equivalent demonstrated depth of experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced proficiency in JavaScript and TypeScript and modern component-based development&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience with a modern component framework such as React or React Native&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience designing and delivering complex, production-scale consumer-facing applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep command of client-side state management and data fetching, including selecting the approach for a codebase rather than working within an existing one&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of application architecture, API design, networking, asynchronous programming and application lifecycle management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience making architectural and technical design decisions for significant features or systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of application performance, reliability, testing, observability and debugging strategies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning performance as a discipline, including measurement, budgets and scope reduction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience identifying and resolving complex technical problems across multiple systems or components&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with CI/CD pipelines, automated testing, release management and version control systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to drive technical and team execution from ambiguous requirements through design, implementation, launch and operational support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to make and influence technical decisions, set priorities, and coordinate engineers and partners toward shared outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience directly managing or formally leading engineers, including coaching, feedback, development, delegation and delivery accountability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong judgment in balancing hands-on technical contribution with people leadership, team capacity and delivery needs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong collaboration and communication skills across Engineering, Product and Design&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional working proficiency in English, with daily collaboration across US-based product and engineering partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or related technical field, or equivalent practical experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing or scaling marketplace, e-commerce, loyalty, or other high-engagement consumer applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading a frontend platform, design-system engineering effort, or small product engineering team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;React Native at scale, or native iOS or Android depth&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with GraphQL, WebSockets, streaming technologies, or other real-time communication patterns&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with analytics, experimentation platforms and observability tooling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience improving frontend architecture or engineering standards across a development team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing delivery for technically complex initiatives involving multiple engineers or partner teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for sports, collectibles, creators, or digital communities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Code-Writing Contribution&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a highly hands-on people leadership role. The Lead Software Engineer is expected to make substantial individual contributions to production code while also being accountable for the execution, technical quality and development of a small cohort of engineers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role will personally solve complex and ambiguous technical problems, contribute to architecture and critical implementation work, and establish engineering patterns that improve scalability, reliability, maintainability and user experience. Hands-on contribution should complement, not replace, effective delegation and team leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to direct code contributions, the Lead Software Engineer sets priorities, coordinates execution, conducts design and code reviews, coaches engineers, provides feedback and development support, removes blockers, and ensures the team delivers against Collector Engagement commitments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Ensure your Fanatics job offer is legitimate and don’t fall victim to fraud.&amp;nbsp; Fanatics never seeks payment from job applicants.&amp;nbsp;Feel free to ask your recruiter for a phone call or other type of communication for interview, and ensure your communication is coming from a Fanatics email address (including @collectfanatics.com).&amp;nbsp; For added security, where possible, apply through our company website at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.fanaticsinc.com/careers&quot;&gt;www.fanaticsinc.com/careers&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By submitting your application, you agree to our terms of service and acknowledge you have read our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://static1.squarespace.com/static/5ff494b9931735466ce28d5b/t/69de53bde2c02c25e9c38758/1776178110037/Candidate+Privacy+Policy+April+2026.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Candidate Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Fanatics will never ask candidates for money, banking information, or other sensitive personal information as part of the interview process. If you receive a suspicious message claiming to be from Fanatics recruiting, please do not respond and report it&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:recruiting-fraud@fanaticsinc.com&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;here&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 class=&quot;job-details__description-header text-color-secondary font-family-secondary&quot; data-bind=&quot;i18n: &#39;job-details.employer-description-title&#39;&quot;&gt;About Us&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;job-details__description-content basic-formatter&quot; data-bind=&quot;html: pageData().job.corporateDescription&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Fanatics is building a leading global digital sports platform. We ignite the passions of global sports fans and maximize the presence and reach for our hundreds of sports partners globally by offering products and services across Fanatics Commerce, Fanatics Collectibles, and Fanatics Betting &amp;amp; Gaming, allowing sports fans to Buy, Collect, and Bet. Through the Fanatics platform, sports fans can buy licensed fan gear, jerseys, lifestyle and streetwear products, headwear, and hardgoods; collect physical and digital trading cards, sports memorabilia, and other digital assets; and bet as the company builds its Sportsbook and iGaming platform. Fanatics has an established database of over 100 million global sports fans; a global partner network with approximately 900 sports properties, including major national and international professional sports leagues, players associations, teams, colleges, college conferences and retail partners, 2,500 athletes and celebrities, and 200 exclusive athletes; and over 2,000 retail locations, including its Lids retail stores. Our more than 22,000 employees are committed to relentlessly enhancing the fan experience and delighting sports fans globally.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fanatics Collectibles is a new company operating at the intersection of collectibles, culture, and technology. Backed by world-class investors, operators, and sports &amp;amp; entertainment partners, we are building the global leader in next-generation collectibles. As part of the broader Fanatics ecosystem, we leverage a digital sports platform that spans over 900 sports properties and engages more than 81 million fans. Together, we are reimagining every part of the collectibles experience for fans, partners, and creators.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fanatics Collectibles is seeking an experienced Legal Director, International to join the Fanatics Collectibles legal team. This is full-time, 5 days on-site role based at Fanatics Collectibles’ UK headquarters in St. Pancras, London, also requiring frequent trips to our office in Milton Keynes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will be cross-functional and support all business groups across all areas of Fanatics Collectibles various businesses outside of the US. You will be a strategic hands-on, results-oriented, business-minded lawyer. You will provide advice on a diverse range of matters related to day-to-day business and operations to all level of team members.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;When determining pay, as part of a final compensation package, we consider several factors such as experience and other qualifications.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Day-to-day responsibilities will include:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rendering advice and guidance regarding legal strategy, interpretation and all legal, compliance and regulatory matters;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drafting, reviewing, and negotiating a broad variety and frequent heavy load of commercial agreements, ranging from the day-to-day/routine to super complex transactions, as well as terms and conditions for merchandise purchases, offerings and products on any scale;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Providing advice and counsel on marketing and promotions matters, including review of contest rules and digital content, including webpages and online promotions;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Engaging, and supervising outside counsel with an eye on careful cost control;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Developing and creating business level appropriate policies controls, procedures and programs;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conducting training related to all responsibility areas.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills, Competencies, and Capabilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;An action and initiative taker;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A “doer” who is ready, willing, and able to roll up sleeves, jump in and &lt;em&gt;&lt;u&gt;get things done&lt;/u&gt;;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A self-starter with a strong work ethic, capable of taking ownership of projects/matters through excellent completion;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have a strong desire to assume a wide variety of responsibilities, learn, stretch, and grow;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to accomplish multiple tasks at once while balancing competing objectives and deadlines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce high-quality carefully crafted work product in a timely manner;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Have strong interpersonal skills and ability to forge strong relationships with key stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work effectively both independently and as a team player in a team oriented environment, friendly, and excited about “play nice” culture;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confident, collaborator and initiative taker, a leader from inception;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Do not watch the clock, be flexible, invested, committed and immersed in the excitement about and commitment to the success of our businesses;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of the Fanatics Collectibles businesses and overall Fanatics current and potential operations;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A creative thinker who can initiate and develop alternative approaches to complex issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A “how” state of mind, not a yes/no advisor;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional and have a non-negotiable sense of integrity, reliable and does the right thing;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent organizational skills and attention to detail;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent legal and business acumen and problem-solving skills;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional communication skills (verbal and written) with the ability to synthesize complex data for a range of audiences. Ability to advise all levels of seniority, summarize the bottom line in a concise manner but also to expand to the full spectrum of details and analysis as appropriate;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Able to function in excellence in a high-paced, entrepreneurial and constantly evolving and fast-moving environment;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Aim and work to be best in class – impactful goal oriented and task focused learner who is innovative and influential;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ambassador of the Fanatics brand who brings passion, energy and positivity into the workplace&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to travel frequently on short notice.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Current Practicing Certificate (UK) or equivalent;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor of Law (LLB) / Masters of Law (LLM) / CPE and Legal Practice Course (LPC);&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years PQE; prior significant in-house experience and/or BigLaw international firm; inhouse experience for a multinational company with US headquarters preferred;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Multi-jurisdictional legal coverage experience preferred;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effective verbal and written communication skills with confidence to communicate with business leaders and all level of employees;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Practical and proactive problem solver with a positive attitude;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in the use and application of AI in a legal environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The above list of job duties is not exclusive or exhaustive and the post holder will be required to undertake such tasks as may reasonably be expected within the scope and grading of the post.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Subject to applicable laws, Fanatics Collectibles may choose to run a background check.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
