&lt;p&gt;Fanatics Collectibles is a new company operating at the intersection of collectibles, culture, and technology. Backed by world-class investors, operators, and sports &amp;amp; entertainment partners, we are building the global leader in next-generation collectibles. As part of the broader Fanatics ecosystem, we leverage a digital sports platform that spans over 900 sports properties and engages more than 81 million fans. Together, we are reimagining every part of the collectibles experience for fans, partners, and creators.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fanatics Collectibles is seeking a Oracle ERP Business Systems Analyst to serve as a functional and technical liaison for the business to design and configure business capabilities and solutions.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years experience with Oracle ERP, knowledge of Oracle SCM and EPM is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep business process knowledge across finance, supply chain (e.g., inventory management, order management, warehouse management, logistics)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and stakeholder management skills, working exceptionally well cross-functionally and with multiple constituents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Become deeply immersed and knowledgeable about core business functions, processes, and workflows associated with assigned business areas and projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with working with business stakeholders to gather business requirements, plan and conduct user acceptance testing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document testing requirements and scripts; oversee testing execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify dependencies and transform process flows into business requirements and technical&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document testing requirements and scripts; oversee testing execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make recommendations for solutions, or improvements, to business processes that can be accomplished through new technology or alternative uses of existing technology&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce timely and high-quality work product requirements including specifications, process flows, mock-ups, and wireframes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in corporate systems in a business analyst type role supporting finance, accounting, FP&amp;amp;A, supply chain, manufacturing and people teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with MS D365 Business Central is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive knowledge of OTC and P2P processes and best practices&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with International operations is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior consulting, transformation or process improvement experience is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Public company experience a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience translating complex technical concepts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in accounting or Information Technology or relevant experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
