&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h1&gt;About Fanatics Collectibles&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fanatics Collectibles is the home of sports cards, trading cards, and collectibles for over 100 million fans worldwide. As part of the global Fanatics platform, we&#39;re rebuilding how collectors discover, buy, sell, and experience their hobby — live, in real time, at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our flagship mobile product, Fanatics Live, is where that experience comes to life: live card breaks, real-time auctions, high-traffic chat, marketplace transactions, and deep collection management tools. The stakes are high and the traffic is real — we build for peak-load moments where latency is visible and reliability is non-negotiable.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;The Role&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll join the &lt;em&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Instant Rips&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/em&gt; Android team — the group responsible for the live-break commerce experience on Fanatics Live.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We build the surfaces millions of collectors use in real time: bidding in live auctions, joining breaks, navigating a high-velocity chat stream, and transacting in the marketplace.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Android stack is modern by design. We build in Kotlin, use Jetpack Compose for declarative UI, and rely on Coroutines and Flow for asynchronous and reactive work. We favor modular, testable architecture with clear dependency boundaries and build against backend services and real-time data streams that must remain reliable during high-traffic events.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AI tooling is part of how we work. We expect engineers to use it on the job, give it good context, and verify the output — not just accept it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and ship production Android features across the live-break experience: auctions, stream viewing, chat, marketplace, and collector tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own features end-to-end — client and API contracts, state and business logic, Compose UI, testing, release, and production health.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build real-time experiences that remain responsive and correct through reconnects, lifecycle changes, degraded networks, and peak-load events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write meaningful test coverage across unit, integration, and UI layers, including deterministic tests for Coroutines, Flow, and failure paths.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve application performance, stability, accessibility, security, and reliability across a broad range of Android devices and OS versions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Diagnose complex production issues using observability, analytics, experimentation, and customer feedback.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review pull requests with judgment: surface real defects, prioritize what matters, and coach on what to let go.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to architectural decisions involving modularization, state management, dependency injection, networking, persistence, and failure handling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Product, Design, backend, iOS, Data, and platform teams to clarify tradeoffs and deliver cohesive customer experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor engineers earlier in their careers and raise the quality bar across the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5+ years&lt;/strong&gt; building and shipping consumer-facing Android applications at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Kotlin&lt;/strong&gt; — deep proficiency with the language and the modern Android ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Jetpack Compose&lt;/strong&gt; — state-aware UI design, navigation, recomposition behavior, accessibility, and performance-conscious composition.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Coroutines and Flow&lt;/strong&gt; — structured concurrency, cancellation, error handling, reactive streams, and lifecycle-aware collection.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Android foundations&lt;/strong&gt; — application and activity lifecycle, configuration changes, process death, networking, persistence, background work, and performance optimization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Architecture&lt;/strong&gt; — experience designing modular, maintainable applications with clear state management, dependency injection, and testable boundaries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;API and real-time integration&lt;/strong&gt; — experience consuming REST or GraphQL services and working with streaming, WebSocket, or subscription-based data patterns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Testing&lt;/strong&gt; — strong unit, integration, and UI testing practices using modern Android testing tools and dependency fakes or mocks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operational excellence&lt;/strong&gt; — hands-on experience with profiling, crash and performance monitoring, analytics, experimentation, and complex production debugging.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Build and release&lt;/strong&gt; — Gradle and CI/CD experience with automated build, test, quality, and release pipelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AI-assisted development&lt;/strong&gt; — practical experience using AI tools to accelerate engineering work while validating correctness, security, and maintainability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior-level ownership&lt;/strong&gt; — a track record of independently delivering complex features, communicating tradeoffs clearly, and mentoring other engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h1&gt;Bonus Points&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with live streaming, real-time auctions, or high-throughput WebSocket or subscription workloads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with marketplace, e-commerce, payments, or other transaction-oriented Android products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting high-scale consumer mobile products during traffic spikes or latency-sensitive events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for sports cards, collectibles, fandom, or live commerce.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Ensure your Fanatics job offer is legitimate and don’t fall victim to fraud.&amp;nbsp; Fanatics never seeks payment from job applicants. Feel free to ask your recruiter for a phone call or other type of communication for interview, and ensure your communication is coming from a Fanatics email address (including @collectfanatics.com).&amp;nbsp; For added security, where possible, apply through our company website at&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.fanaticsinc.com/careers&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s2&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;www.fanaticsinc.com/careers&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The salary range represents base pay only and does not include short-term or long-term incentive compensation. &amp;nbsp;This salary range is specific to New York City and may not be applicable to other locations. &amp;nbsp;When determining base pay, as part of a final compensation package, we consider several factors such as location, experience, qualifications, and training. For information about our benefits, please visit&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://benefitsatfanatics.com/&quot;&gt;https://benefitsatfanatics.com/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;NYC Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$160,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$200,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By submitting your application, you agree to our terms of service and acknowledge you have read our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://static1.squarespace.com/static/5ff494b9931735466ce28d5b/t/69de53bde2c02c25e9c38758/1776178110037/Candidate+Privacy+Policy+April+2026.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Candidate Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Fanatics will never ask candidates for money, banking information, or other sensitive personal information as part of the interview process. If you receive a suspicious message claiming to be from Fanatics recruiting, please do not respond and report it&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:recruiting-fraud@fanaticsinc.com&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;here&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 class=&quot;job-details__description-header text-color-secondary font-family-secondary&quot; data-bind=&quot;i18n: &#39;job-details.employer-description-title&#39;&quot;&gt;About Us&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;job-details__description-content basic-formatter&quot; data-bind=&quot;html: pageData().job.corporateDescription&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Fanatics is building a leading global digital sports platform. We ignite the passions of global sports fans and maximize the presence and reach for our hundreds of sports partners globally by offering products and services across Fanatics Commerce, Fanatics Collectibles, and Fanatics Betting &amp;amp; Gaming, allowing sports fans to Buy, Collect, and Bet. Through the Fanatics platform, sports fans can buy licensed fan gear, jerseys, lifestyle and streetwear products, headwear, and hardgoods; collect physical and digital trading cards, sports memorabilia, and other digital assets; and bet as the company builds its Sportsbook and iGaming platform. Fanatics has an established database of over 100 million global sports fans; a global partner network with approximately 900 sports properties, including major national and international professional sports leagues, players associations, teams, colleges, college conferences and retail partners, 2,500 athletes and celebrities, and 200 exclusive athletes; and over 2,000 retail locations, including its Lids retail stores. Our more than 22,000 employees are committed to relentlessly enhancing the fan experience and delighting sports fans globally.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Fanatics Collectibles&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fanatics Collectibles is the home of sports cards, trading cards, and collectibles for over 100 million fans worldwide. As part of the global Fanatics platform, we’re rebuilding how collectors discover, buy, sell, and experience their hobby — live, in real time, at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Collectors move between live breaks, instant rips, auctions, the marketplace, and their collection every day. Currently, those are sometimes distinct experiences and separate apps. Our work is to bring these experiences together as a single product and build new ways for collectors to discover what they’re looking for.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll join the&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Unified Experience / Discovery&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;team, a new group responsible for building seamless collector journeys &amp;amp; discovery across Fanatics Live, Marketplace, Instant Rips, Collections, Topps, and future experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As the first Android developer on a new team, you’ll be responsible for underlying architecture as we bring existing, separate services closer together. You will also help implement new user-facing features we will build on top of that unified structure. This is a high-impact role with significant ownership, and the work will require collaboration with stakeholders across the organization, including other engineering teams (which may be downstream consumers of your work), product leaders, and other business roles.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Android stack is modern by design: Kotlin and Jetpack Compose throughout, Coroutines and Flow for concurrency and state, a unidirectional architecture with a strict state contract, GraphQL against our backend, and a modular multi-module Gradle codebase with automated build and release pipelines.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AI tooling is part of how we work. We expect engineers to leverage it, have a productive workflow, understand the code produced, and own the results.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and ship shared Android foundations — reusable modules, Compose components, and internal libraries — that multiple collector-facing apps depend on, and treat the engineers consuming them as first-class customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own unified identity, session, and entitlement flows across surfaces, so a collector signs in once and moves between Live, Instant Rips, Marketplace, and Collections without friction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead migrations and consolidations against live users: persistence and data model changes, deprecating divergent implementations, and phased rollouts that don’t break anyone mid-flow.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own features end to end — API contracts, state and effect handling, Compose UI, testing, and release.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build deep linking, navigation, and cross-surface handoffs that make separate products behave like one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write genuine test coverage: unit tests with fake dependencies, Flow and coroutine test patterns, Compose UI tests where they earn their keep — not coverage theater.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Instrument what you ship and watch it in production: event tracking, feature flags, staged Play Store rollouts, crash and ANR triage, and monitoring you actually check after launch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own Android performance where users feel it: startup time, jank in scrolling and animation-heavy surfaces, memory under sustained real-time load.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review pull requests with judgment: surface real defects, prioritize what matters, coach on what to let go.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to architectural decisions: modularization strategy, state management, effect handling, failure handling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor engineers earlier in their career and raise the quality bar across the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we’re looking for&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5+ years&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;building consumer-facing Android applications at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Kotlin&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;— coroutines, structured concurrency, Flow, and a working understanding of where each belongs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Jetpack Compose&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;— state hoisting, recomposition and stability, performance-aware composition, Compose Navigation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Unidirectional state management at scale&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;— MVI or a comparable strict, testable architecture (Molecule, Orbit, Mavericks, or a well-reasoned in-house pattern) that you can explain and defend.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Multi-module Gradle architecture&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;— clean module boundaries, convention plugins, version catalogs, build times you’ve actively fought for.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Shared architecture across multiple apps&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;— you’ve built reusable modules, SDKs, or internal libraries consumed by more than one app or more than one team, and you understand the API-stability and versioning discipline that requires.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Dependency injection&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;— Hilt, Dagger, Koin, or equivalent, used deliberately rather than by habit.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;GraphQL on Android&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;— Apollo Kotlin, schema-driven development, codegen, subscriptions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CI/CD&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;— Bitrise, GitHub Actions, Fastlane, or equivalent automated build/test/release pipelines feeding the Play Console.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Testing discipline&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;— JUnit, Turbine, Robolectric, Compose testing, and instrumentation tests, with real assertions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Static analysis&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;— ktlint, detekt, or equivalent quality gates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hands-on with AI-assisted development tooling&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;— Claude Code, Cursor, Copilot, or similar — with a track record of using it for real work, not demos.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Structured commit/PR discipline&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;tied to a project tracker (Linear, Jira, or equivalent).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working across team boundaries — this role depends on influence with engineers you don’t manage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Bonus points&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with livestreaming, real-time auctions, or high-throughput WebSocket/subscription workloads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Baseline Profiles, Macrobenchmark, or other systematic Android performance work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to marketplace or e-commerce Android applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Payments, billing, or Play Billing experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Developer tooling or internal platform work that measurably saved other engineers time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for sports cards, collectibles, or live commerce.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Ensure your Fanatics job offer is legitimate and don’t fall victim to fraud.&amp;nbsp; Fanatics never seeks payment from job applicants. Feel free to ask your recruiter for a phone call or other type of communication for interview, and ensure your communication is coming from a Fanatics email address (including @collectfanatics.com).&amp;nbsp; For added security, where possible, apply through our company website at&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.fanaticsinc.com/careers&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s2&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;www.fanaticsinc.com/careers&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The salary range represents base pay only and does not include short-term or long-term incentive compensation. &amp;nbsp;This salary range is specific to Los Angeles and may not be applicable to other locations. &amp;nbsp;When determining base pay, as part of a final compensation package, we consider several factors such as location, experience, qualifications, and training. For information about our benefits, please visit&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://benefitsatfanatics.com/&quot;&gt;https://benefitsatfanatics.com/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Los Angeles Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$144,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$180,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The salary range represents base pay only and does not include short-term or long-term incentive compensation. &amp;nbsp;This salary range is specific to New York City and may not be applicable to other locations. &amp;nbsp;When determining base pay, as part of a final compensation package, we consider several factors such as location, experience, qualifications, and training. For information about our benefits, please visit&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://benefitsatfanatics.com/&quot;&gt;https://benefitsatfanatics.com/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;NYC Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$160,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$200,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By submitting your application, you agree to our terms of service and acknowledge you have read our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://static1.squarespace.com/static/5ff494b9931735466ce28d5b/t/69de53bde2c02c25e9c38758/1776178110037/Candidate+Privacy+Policy+April+2026.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Candidate Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Fanatics will never ask candidates for money, banking information, or other sensitive personal information as part of the interview process. If you receive a suspicious message claiming to be from Fanatics recruiting, please do not respond and report it&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:recruiting-fraud@fanaticsinc.com&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;here&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 class=&quot;job-details__description-header text-color-secondary font-family-secondary&quot; data-bind=&quot;i18n: &#39;job-details.employer-description-title&#39;&quot;&gt;About Us&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;job-details__description-content basic-formatter&quot; data-bind=&quot;html: pageData().job.corporateDescription&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Fanatics is building a leading global digital sports platform. We ignite the passions of global sports fans and maximize the presence and reach for our hundreds of sports partners globally by offering products and services across Fanatics Commerce, Fanatics Collectibles, and Fanatics Betting &amp;amp; Gaming, allowing sports fans to Buy, Collect, and Bet. Through the Fanatics platform, sports fans can buy licensed fan gear, jerseys, lifestyle and streetwear products, headwear, and hardgoods; collect physical and digital trading cards, sports memorabilia, and other digital assets; and bet as the company builds its Sportsbook and iGaming platform. Fanatics has an established database of over 100 million global sports fans; a global partner network with approximately 900 sports properties, including major national and international professional sports leagues, players associations, teams, colleges, college conferences and retail partners, 2,500 athletes and celebrities, and 200 exclusive athletes; and over 2,000 retail locations, including its Lids retail stores. Our more than 22,000 employees are committed to relentlessly enhancing the fan experience and delighting sports fans globally.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;Fanatics Collectibles is a new company operating at the intersection of collectibles, culture, and technology. Backed by world-class investors, operators, and sports &amp;amp; entertainment partners, we are building the global leader in next-generation collectibles. As part of the broader Fanatics ecosystem, we leverage a digital sports platform that spans over 900 sports properties and engages more than 81 million fans. Together, we are reimagining every part of the collectibles experience for fans, partners, and creators.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;About the Role&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Senior Engineer, DevOps to join the Live &amp;amp; Collect Infrastructure team in Los Angeles. You&#39;ll design, build, and operate the cloud foundation that powers Fanatics&#39; Live &amp;amp; Collect platforms across AWS and GCP. This is a hands-on role for someone who enjoys solving hard infrastructure problems at scale, applying AI/ML tooling to infrastructure and operations, mentoring other engineers, and championing DevOps maturity across the org.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, and maintain scalable, resilient infrastructure across AWS and GCP using infrastructure-as-code (Terraform).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own core cloud platform services — Kubernetes, networking, and CI/CD pipelines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate and integrate AI-assisted tooling (e.g., LLM-based automation, AIOps, intelligent monitoring) to improve infrastructure efficiency and operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with product and platform engineering teams to architect cloud solutions that support high-traffic, high-availability Live &amp;amp; Collect systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Administer and tune managed and self-hosted databases (Cloud Spanner, AWS RDS, PostgreSQL), including performance tuning, capacity planning, backup/recovery, and query optimization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive reliability and cost-efficiency initiatives across multi-cloud environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Champion DevOps best practices, scalable infrastructure patterns, and observability standards across engineering teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor engineers on cloud architecture, automation, and operational excellence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in an on-call rotation, responding to and resolving production incidents to meet SLAs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to security hardening, compliance, and disaster-recovery planning for cloud infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in cloud engineering, infrastructure, or SRE roles, with production experience in both AWS and GCP.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong background with infrastructure-as-code (Terraform preferred) and container orchestration (Kubernetes).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on database administration and tuning experience with Cloud Spanner, AWS RDS, and PostgreSQL (performance tuning, replication, backup/recovery, capacity planning).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with CI/CD tooling and modern DevOps automation practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with AI/ML-powered tooling for infrastructure automation, monitoring, or operations (e.g., AIOps platforms, LLM-based automation, copilots for infra/ops workflows).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid scripting/programming ability (Python, Go, or similar) for automation and tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience operating and troubleshooting large-scale, distributed, high-availability systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable carrying on-call responsibilities and driving incidents to resolution under pressure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills and experience mentoring other engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Computer Science, Engineering, or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting live events, auctions, or other high-traffic consumer platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience building or integrating AI/ML pipelines or infrastructure for AI workloads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relevant cloud certifications (AWS or GCP).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with cost optimization and FinOps practices across multi-cloud environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Ensure your Fanatics job offer is legitimate and don’t fall victim to fraud.&amp;nbsp; Fanatics never seeks payment from job applicants.&amp;nbsp;Feel free to ask your recruiter for a phone call or other type of communication for interview, and ensure your communication is coming from a Fanatics email address (including @collectfanatics.com).&amp;nbsp; For added security, where possible, apply through our company website at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.fanaticsinc.com/careers&quot;&gt;www.fanaticsinc.com/careers&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The salary range represents base pay only and does not include short-term or long-term incentive compensation. &amp;nbsp;This salary range is specific to Los Angeles and may not be applicable to other locations. &amp;nbsp;When determining base pay, as part of a final compensation package, we consider several factors such as location, experience, qualifications, and training. For information about our benefits, please visit&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://benefitsatfanatics.com/&quot;&gt;https://benefitsatfanatics.com/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;Los Angeles Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$144,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$180,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By submitting your application, you agree to our terms of service and acknowledge you have read our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://static1.squarespace.com/static/5ff494b9931735466ce28d5b/t/69de53bde2c02c25e9c38758/1776178110037/Candidate+Privacy+Policy+April+2026.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Candidate Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Fanatics will never ask candidates for money, banking information, or other sensitive personal information as part of the interview process. If you receive a suspicious message claiming to be from Fanatics recruiting, please do not respond and report it&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:recruiting-fraud@fanaticsinc.com&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;here&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 class=&quot;job-details__description-header text-color-secondary font-family-secondary&quot; data-bind=&quot;i18n: &#39;job-details.employer-description-title&#39;&quot;&gt;About Us&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;job-details__description-content basic-formatter&quot; data-bind=&quot;html: pageData().job.corporateDescription&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Fanatics is building a leading global digital sports platform. We ignite the passions of global sports fans and maximize the presence and reach for our hundreds of sports partners globally by offering products and services across Fanatics Commerce, Fanatics Collectibles, and Fanatics Betting &amp;amp; Gaming, allowing sports fans to Buy, Collect, and Bet. Through the Fanatics platform, sports fans can buy licensed fan gear, jerseys, lifestyle and streetwear products, headwear, and hardgoods; collect physical and digital trading cards, sports memorabilia, and other digital assets; and bet as the company builds its Sportsbook and iGaming platform. Fanatics has an established database of over 100 million global sports fans; a global partner network with approximately 900 sports properties, including major national and international professional sports leagues, players associations, teams, colleges, college conferences and retail partners, 2,500 athletes and celebrities, and 200 exclusive athletes; and over 2,000 retail locations, including its Lids retail stores. Our more than 22,000 employees are committed to relentlessly enhancing the fan experience and delighting sports fans globally.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fanatics Collectibles is the home of sports cards, trading cards, and collectibles for over 100 million fans worldwide. As part of the global Fanatics platform, we&#39;re rebuilding how collectors discover, buy, sell, and experience their hobby — live, in real time, at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our flagship mobile product, &lt;strong&gt;Fanatics Live&lt;/strong&gt;, is where that experience comes to life: live card breaks, real-time auctions, high-traffic chat, marketplace transactions, and deep collection management tools. The stakes are high and the traffic is real — we build for peak-load moments where latency is visible and reliability is nonnegotiable.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll join the &lt;strong&gt;Instant Rips&lt;/strong&gt; iOS team — the group responsible for the live-break commerce experience on Fanatics Live. We build the surfaces millions of collectors use in real time: bidding in live auctions, joining breaks, navigating a high-velocity chat stream, and transacting in the marketplace.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The iOS stack is modern by design. We&#39;re SwiftUI-first, run The Composable Architecture TCA) across the app, use Swift Concurrency throughout, talk to our backend via Apollo GraphQL, and maintain a clean modular SPM codebase generated with Tuist. There&#39;s no legacy UIKit app hiding under the surface — you&#39;ll be working in a codebase you can be proud of.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;AI tooling is part of how we work. We expect engineers to use it on the job, give it good context, and verify the output — not just accept it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What you&#39;ll do&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and ship production iOS features across the live-break experience: auctions, stream viewing, chat, marketplace, and collector tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own features end-to-end — API contracts, TCA reducers, SwiftUI views, testing, and release&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write genuine test coverage: unit tests with mock dependencies, TCA&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;TestStore assertions, async test patterns — not coverage theater&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review pull requests with judgment: surface real defects, prioritize what matters, coach on what to let go&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to architectural decisions: modularization strategy, effect management, failure handling&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor engineers earlier in their career and raise the quality bar across the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What we&#39;re looking for&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;5+ years&lt;/strong&gt; building consumer-facing iOS applications at scale&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on with AI-assisted development tooling LLM optimization loops,&amp;nbsp;Xcode CLI integration)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Swift Concurrency&lt;/strong&gt; — async/await, structured concurrency, Sendable, Swift&amp;nbsp;Macros&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SwiftUI&lt;/strong&gt; — stateless/stateful view patterns, NavigationStack, performanceaware composition&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Composable Architecture TCA&lt;/strong&gt; — Reducer/Store/Action/State, effect management, parent-child delegation, testing with TestStore&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Apollo GraphQL (iOS)&lt;/strong&gt; — schema-driven development, Swift codegen, subscriptions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SPM multi-package architecture&lt;/strong&gt; — modular feature separation, local packages, clean dependency graphs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Tuist or XcodeGen&lt;/strong&gt; — project generation tooling; no committed &lt;sub&gt;.xcodeproj &lt;/sub&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CI/CD&lt;/strong&gt; — Bitrise, Fastlane, or equivalent automated build/test pipelines &lt;strong&gt;Static analysis&lt;/strong&gt; — SwiftLint, Periphery or equivalent code quality gates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Structured commit/PR discipline&lt;/strong&gt; tied to a project tracker Linear, Jira, or equivalent)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Bonus points&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with livestreaming, real-time auctions, or high-throughput WebSocket/subscription workloads&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to marketplace or e-commerce iOS applications&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for sports cards, collectibles, or live commerce&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The above list of job duties is not exclusive or exhaustive and the post holder will be required to undertake such tasks as may reasonably be expected within the scope and grading of the post.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Subject to applicable laws, Fanatics Collectibles may choose to run a background check.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Ensure your Fanatics job offer is legitimate and don’t fall victim to fraud.&amp;nbsp; Fanatics never seeks payment from job applicants.&amp;nbsp;Feel free to ask your recruiter for a phone call or other type of communication for interview, and ensure your communication is coming from a Fanatics email address (including @collectfanatics.com).&amp;nbsp; For added security, where possible, apply through our company website at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.fanaticsinc.com/careers&quot;&gt;www.fanaticsinc.com/careers&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By submitting your application, you agree to our terms of service and acknowledge you have read our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://static1.squarespace.com/static/5ff494b9931735466ce28d5b/t/69de53bde2c02c25e9c38758/1776178110037/Candidate+Privacy+Policy+April+2026.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Candidate Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Fanatics will never ask candidates for money, banking information, or other sensitive personal information as part of the interview process. If you receive a suspicious message claiming to be from Fanatics recruiting, please do not respond and report it&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:recruiting-fraud@fanaticsinc.com&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;here&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
