&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 class=&quot;job-details__description-header text-color-secondary font-family-secondary&quot; data-bind=&quot;i18n: &#39;job-details.employer-description-title&#39;&quot;&gt;About Us&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;job-details__description-content basic-formatter&quot; data-bind=&quot;html: pageData().job.corporateDescription&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Fanatics is building a leading global digital sports platform. We ignite the passions of global sports fans and maximize the presence and reach for our hundreds of sports partners globally by offering products and services across Fanatics Commerce, Fanatics Collectibles, and Fanatics Betting &amp;amp; Gaming, allowing sports fans to Buy, Collect, and Bet. Through the Fanatics platform, sports fans can buy licensed fan gear, jerseys, lifestyle and streetwear products, headwear, and hardgoods; collect physical and digital trading cards, sports memorabilia, and other digital assets; and bet as the company builds its Sportsbook and iGaming platform. Fanatics has an established database of over 100 million global sports fans; a global partner network with approximately 900 sports properties, including major national and international professional sports leagues, players associations, teams, colleges, college conferences and retail partners, 2,500 athletes and celebrities, and 200 exclusive athletes; and over 2,000 retail locations, including its Lids retail stores. Our more than 22,000 employees are committed to relentlessly enhancing the fan experience and delighting sports fans globally.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fanatics Collectibles is a new company operating at the intersection of collectibles, culture, and technology. Backed by world-class investors, operators, and sports &amp;amp; entertainment partners, we are building the global leader in next-generation collectibles. As part of the broader Fanatics ecosystem, we leverage a digital sports platform that spans over 900 sports properties and engages more than 81 million fans. Together, we are reimagining every part of the collectibles experience for fans, partners, and creators.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fanatics Collect is building a trusted marketplace where collectors can securely store, discover, buy, and sell trading cards. We are seeking a Senior Full Stack Engineer to develop the customer experiences and platform capabilities that power the Collect marketplace, including Vault, Buy Now, auctions, and the tooling used to manage marketplace operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will own complex features across the technology stack, from intuitive web experiences to scalable services and data models. You will partner with product, design, operations, and engineering teams to deliver reliable marketplace experiences that make collecting easier, faster, and more engaging.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As part of Fanatics Collectibles’ continued global growth, we are establishing a new technology hub in Mexico City focused on operational excellence, platform scalability, trust, and customer experience. This team partners closely with Customer Experience (CX), Trust &amp;amp; Safety, Fraud Prevention, Payments, and Financial Operations organizations to build scalable systems and operational tooling that support millions of users and transactions globally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, test, deploy, and operate full-stack features supporting Vault, Buy Now, auctions, and marketplace tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop intuitive customer experiences for managing vaulted assets, creating listings, placing bids, purchasing collectibles, and tracking transactions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build scalable backend services and APIs that support marketplace workflows, inventory, listings, bidding, and order lifecycles.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strengthen the reliability and integrity of time-sensitive and transaction-heavy experiences, including live auctions and high-demand product activity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate complex marketplace and operational requirements into maintainable technical solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with product managers and designers to shape requirements, evaluate tradeoffs, and deliver high-quality customer experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with platform, infrastructure, data, security, and other engineering teams to build integrated solutions across the Collect ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Improve application performance, observability, testing, deployment practices, and production readiness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Diagnose complex production issues, contribute to incident response, and drive root-cause fixes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish reusable patterns and engineering practices that improve the quality and velocity of full-stack development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide thoughtful code reviews, technical guidance, and mentorship to other engineers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to architectural decisions and help evolve the marketplace technology roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We’re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Five or more years of professional software engineering experience, including meaningful ownership of full-stack applications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong experience building modern web applications using technologies such as React, TypeScript, or comparable frameworks and languages.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing backend services and APIs using languages and frameworks such as Node.js, Java, Kotlin, Go, Python, or similar technologies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of data modeling and experience working with relational or non-relational databases.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience designing and operating scalable, reliable, customer-facing systems in a production environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of distributed systems, asynchronous processing, caching, and event-driven architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with automated testing, continuous integration and delivery, observability, and cloud-based deployment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to break down ambiguous problems, make sound technical decisions, and deliver solutions across multiple systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong product judgment and an appreciation for how technical decisions affect customers and business operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear communication skills and the ability to collaborate effectively across engineering, product, design, and operational teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building e-commerce, marketplace, fintech, auction, inventory, or other transaction-oriented products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing real-time or time-sensitive functionality, such as bidding, pricing, notifications, or live-event experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with payments, order management, fulfillment, identity, fraud prevention, or marketplace trust and safety.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting internal operational tools alongside external customer experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest in trading cards, collectibles, marketplaces, or collector communities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How You’ll Make an Impact&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will help shape the technology that connects physical collectibles with digital marketplace experiences. Your work will enable collectors to confidently manage vaulted assets, participate in auctions, purchase cards, and engage with the Collect marketplace at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Ensure your Fanatics job offer is legitimate and don’t fall victim to fraud.&amp;nbsp; Fanatics never seeks payment from job applicants.&amp;nbsp;Feel free to ask your recruiter for a phone call or other type of communication for interview, and ensure your communication is coming from a Fanatics email address (including @collectfanatics.com).&amp;nbsp; For added security, where possible, apply through our company website at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.fanaticsinc.com/careers&quot;&gt;www.fanaticsinc.com/careers&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By submitting your application, you agree to our terms of service and acknowledge you have read our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://static1.squarespace.com/static/5ff494b9931735466ce28d5b/t/69de53bde2c02c25e9c38758/1776178110037/Candidate+Privacy+Policy+April+2026.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Candidate Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Fanatics will never ask candidates for money, banking information, or other sensitive personal information as part of the interview process. If you receive a suspicious message claiming to be from Fanatics recruiting, please do not respond and report it&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:recruiting-fraud@fanaticsinc.com&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;here&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 class=&quot;job-details__description-header text-color-secondary font-family-secondary&quot; data-bind=&quot;i18n: &#39;job-details.employer-description-title&#39;&quot;&gt;About Us&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;job-details__description-content basic-formatter&quot; data-bind=&quot;html: pageData().job.corporateDescription&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Fanatics is building a leading global digital sports platform. We ignite the passions of global sports fans and maximize the presence and reach for our hundreds of sports partners globally by offering products and services across Fanatics Commerce, Fanatics Collectibles, and Fanatics Betting &amp;amp; Gaming, allowing sports fans to Buy, Collect, and Bet. Through the Fanatics platform, sports fans can buy licensed fan gear, jerseys, lifestyle and streetwear products, headwear, and hardgoods; collect physical and digital trading cards, sports memorabilia, and other digital assets; and bet as the company builds its Sportsbook and iGaming platform. Fanatics has an established database of over 100 million global sports fans; a global partner network with approximately 900 sports properties, including major national and international professional sports leagues, players associations, teams, colleges, college conferences and retail partners, 2,500 athletes and celebrities, and 200 exclusive athletes; and over 2,000 retail locations, including its Lids retail stores. Our more than 22,000 employees are committed to relentlessly enhancing the fan experience and delighting sports fans globally.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Support Fanatics Collect’s Unified Experience / Discovery initiative, building seamless collector journeys across Fanatics Live, Marketplace, Instant Rips, Collections, Topps, and future experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Today a collector can win a card in a live show, rip a pack, buy on the marketplace, and store it all in a vault but those moments still feel like separate products. Your job will be to make them feel like one. That means building the shared surfaces, APIs, and front-end systems that connect experiences that were each built independently, and doing it without slowing any of them down.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hands-on senior role on a new team, with significant ownership of the shared architecture that will bring these experiences together. You’ll help shape that foundation and build new features on top of it, owning the work end to end. The team is currently small but growing and, as part of it, you’ll get a chance to collaborate closely with other engineering teams, product leadership, design, and other business stakeholders.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why Join Us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fanatics Collect is growing fast, and the unification work is the highest-leverage engineering investment we have: every new app, drop, and live format gets easier once the shared foundation exists. You’ll work across mobile, web, and internal tools, with real autonomy and a short path from idea to production. Your teammates are passionate about the space and most of them are collectors themselves.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product Context and Scale&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our surfaces reach millions of collectors across iOS, Android, and web, with live, high-traffic moments (breaks, drops, auctions closing) that make performance and reliability non-negotiable. You’ll be working in a landscape of multiple existing products with real users and real data, so migration, backward compatibility, and careful rollout are part of the craft.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;First 90 Days&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ship a meaningful, user-facing piece of the unified experience end to end.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build a working map of how Live, Marketplace, Instant Rips, Collections, and Topps actually fit together today — data models, identity, entitlements, and the seams between them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish working relationships with the backend, mobile, product, and design partners you’ll depend on.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify one piece of duplicated or divergent logic across surfaces and make the case for consolidating it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, build, and maintain fullstack features using Python, FastAPI, Next.js, React, and TypeScript.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build scalable, performant, highly available services and interfaces on AWS and Vercel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own features end to end: data model, API contract, front-end implementation, tests, rollout, and post-launch metrics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain reusable front-end components, APIs, and shared libraries that multiple apps (web and mobile) depend on — and treat other engineers as first-class consumers of what you build.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to cross-surface concerns like shared identity, entitlements, inventory, and navigation between collector experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ship behind feature flags with instrumentation in place, and use the resulting data to decide what to keep, fix, or cut.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prototype quickly with Product and Design when a working demo will settle a debate faster than a document.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use AI-assisted development tools (Claude Code, Cursor, LLM-backed workflows) to raise your own throughput, and share what works with the team.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Write meaningful tests across the stack — unit, integration, and E2E — using Playwright, Jest, React Testing Library, and Pytest, and keep CI/CD pipelines trustworthy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain component documentation and interaction specs via Storybook.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in sprint planning, retros, and product strategy sessions; raise scope and sequencing concerns early rather than at the end.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor engineers through code review and pairing, and raise the bar on code structure, testing, and documentation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of professional fullstack development experience, with demonstrated proficiency in React, Next.js, TypeScript, and Python, plus hands-on cloud experience (AWS preferred).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong grasp of architectural patterns, API design, and application performance tuning — and the judgment to know when a simpler solution is the right one.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of owning features end to end in production, including the parts after launch: monitoring, debugging, and iterating on real user behavior.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solid front-end fundamentals: responsive UI development, accessibility (a11y), and front-end performance practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with state management patterns and tools such as React Context, Zustand, Redux, or XState, and a thoughtful approach to complexity in large apps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong testing discipline with tools such as Jest, React Testing Library, Playwright, or Pytest.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with Git and modern CI/CD practices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable working across domains — backend APIs, customer-facing web, mobile web, and internal tools — and context switching without dropping threads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear written and verbal communication; able to work directly with Product, Design, and other engineering teams and drive alignment on your own work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using or a genuine appetite for AI developer tooling to improve velocity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Computer Science or equivalent practical experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to Have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience integrating or consolidating multiple existing products, including data migrations against live users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with high-traffic, real-time, or live-event product surfaces.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in growth engineering or rapid experimentation frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in e-commerce, marketplaces, or gaming live ops.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design system or shared component library ownership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for collecting, trading, sports, or gaming — and an interest in being a user of what you build.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you like owning problems end to end, care about how software feels and not just whether it works, and want your work used daily by millions of collectors — we’d love to talk.&lt;/p&gt;
