&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 class=&quot;job-details__description-header text-color-secondary font-family-secondary&quot; data-bind=&quot;i18n: &#39;job-details.employer-description-title&#39;&quot;&gt;About Us&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;job-details__description-content basic-formatter&quot; data-bind=&quot;html: pageData().job.corporateDescription&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Fanatics is building a leading global digital sports platform. We ignite the passions of global sports fans and maximize the presence and reach for our hundreds of sports partners globally by offering products and services across Fanatics Commerce, Fanatics Collectibles, and Fanatics Betting &amp;amp; Gaming, allowing sports fans to Buy, Collect, and Bet. Through the Fanatics platform, sports fans can buy licensed fan gear, jerseys, lifestyle and streetwear products, headwear, and hardgoods; collect physical and digital trading cards, sports memorabilia, and other digital assets; and bet as the company builds its Sportsbook and iGaming platform. Fanatics has an established database of over 100 million global sports fans; a global partner network with approximately 900 sports properties, including major national and international professional sports leagues, players associations, teams, colleges, college conferences and retail partners, 2,500 athletes and celebrities, and 200 exclusive athletes; and over 2,000 retail locations, including its Lids retail stores. Our more than 22,000 employees are committed to relentlessly enhancing the fan experience and delighting sports fans globally.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Company&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Fanatics Collectibles is a new company operating at the intersection of collectibles, culture, and technology. Backed by world-class investors, operators, and sports &amp;amp; entertainment partners, we are building the global leader in next-generation collectibles. As part of the broader Fanatics ecosystem, we leverage a digital sports platform that spans over 900 sports properties and engages more than 81 million fans. Together, we are reimagining every part of the collectibles experience for fans, partners, and creators.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Fanatics Collectibles is hiring a Senior Manager, Business Operations to help plan, build, launch, and &lt;strong&gt;scale a new U.S. manufacturing facility in the Atlanta or Indianapolis market&lt;/strong&gt;. Reporting to the Senior Director, Transformation, this person will be a core member of the launch team and the day-to-day program leader connecting internal functions with real estate, design and construction, equipment, and other external partners.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The role will initially be based at our Texas facilities, primarily in Sunnyvale, Allen, or Coppell - to allow local flexibility&lt;/strong&gt;, where the Senior Manager will learn our end-to-end operating model and help lead site planning, lease execution, design, buildout, and launch preparation. &lt;strong&gt;The position will transition to the selected market (Indianapolis or Atlanta&lt;/strong&gt;) once the facility shell is substantially complete and the work shifts onsite to equipment installation, commissioning, hiring, training, operational readiness, and startup. After launch, this person will remain at the new facility as a strategic and operating partner to site leadership, helping the operation stabilize, scale, and achieve operational excellence.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;Within the first 6-12 months, you will...&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Embed in our Texas operations to understand the end-to-end manufacturing system, document critical controls and lessons learned, and convert them into clear requirements and a practical launch playbook for the new site.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Build and manage the integrated master plan for the facility launch, including scope, critical path, budget, stage gates, workstream dependencies, risks, decisions, and executive governance.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Coordinate internal teams and external partners through site and lease diligence, facility programming and design, permitting, utilities, construction, IT, security, environmental health and safety, quality, and buildout readiness.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Partner with Engineering, Manufacturing, equipment suppliers, and contractors to define layout, material flow, and equipment requirements and to coordinate procurement, delivery, installation, commissioning, qualification, and handoff to operations.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Translate demand and capacity requirements into the operating design, including production flow, shift and labor models, organization and hiring plans, supply chain, logistics, warehousing, and inventory strategy.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Coordinate systems and data readiness, including ERP, production and warehouse systems, master data, integrations, operating reports, and KPI dashboards required to run the new facility effectively from day one.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Establish the knowledge-transfer and change-management approach, including standard work, SOPs, training and certification, and clear process ownership so the new team can reproduce and improve upon proven Texas practices.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Transition to the new site as the facility moves from shell completion into onsite execution, then lead launch and ramp governance, rapid issue resolution, and performance management across safety, quality, service, cost, and output.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;em&gt;The Ideal Candidate:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Ability to work onsite at our Texas facilities, &lt;strong&gt;primarily in Sunnyvale, Allen, or Coppell, at the start of the role&lt;/strong&gt;; travel regularly to the selected market during design and construction; &lt;strong&gt;and relocate to &lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Atlanta&lt;/span&gt; or &lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;Indianapolis&lt;/span&gt; when onsite equipment installation and launch work begins.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;7-10 years of experience in management consulting, business operations, complex program management, industrial or manufacturing engineering, manufacturing operations, or supply chain. Experience supporting or leading a factory launch, major expansion, equipment installation, or comparable capital program is required; direct greenfield experience is strongly preferred.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in engineering, supply chain, operations, business, finance, economics, or a related field; MBA or relevant master&#39;s degree preferred.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Demonstrated ability to create structure from ambiguity and lead large, interdependent programs with clear plans, governance, accountability, financial discipline, and executive-level communication.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Practical knowledge of manufacturing and facility operations, including equipment life cycles, capacity and production planning, material flow, workforce planning, quality, safety, logistics, and supply chain.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Strong quantitative modeling, analytical, and financial skills, with the ability to build business cases, evaluate scenarios, identify tradeoffs, and translate insights into operating decisions.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication skills, sound judgment, and the ability to influence senior leaders, operators, technical teams, vendors, and external partners without relying on direct authority.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Hands-on, team-first leadership style with high ownership, comfort spending time on the manufacturing floor, and a bias toward execution, problem solving, and continuous improvement.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Ensure your Fanatics job offer is legitimate and don’t fall victim to fraud.&amp;nbsp; Fanatics never seeks payment from job applicants. Feel free to ask your recruiter for a phone call or other type of communication for interview, and ensure your communication is coming from a Fanatics email address (including @collectfanatics.com).&amp;nbsp; For added security, where possible, apply through our company website at &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.fanaticsinc.com/careers&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s2&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;www.fanaticsinc.com/careers&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By submitting your application, you agree to our terms of service and acknowledge you have read our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://static1.squarespace.com/static/5ff494b9931735466ce28d5b/t/69de53bde2c02c25e9c38758/1776178110037/Candidate+Privacy+Policy+April+2026.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Candidate Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Fanatics will never ask candidates for money, banking information, or other sensitive personal information as part of the interview process. If you receive a suspicious message claiming to be from Fanatics recruiting, please do not respond and report it&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:recruiting-fraud@fanaticsinc.com&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;here&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 class=&quot;job-details__description-header text-color-secondary font-family-secondary&quot; data-bind=&quot;i18n: &#39;job-details.employer-description-title&#39;&quot;&gt;About Us&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;job-details__description-content basic-formatter&quot; data-bind=&quot;html: pageData().job.corporateDescription&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Fanatics is building a leading global digital sports platform. We ignite the passions of global sports fans and maximize the presence and reach for our hundreds of sports partners globally by offering products and services across Fanatics Commerce, Fanatics Collectibles, and Fanatics Betting &amp;amp; Gaming, allowing sports fans to Buy, Collect, and Bet. Through the Fanatics platform, sports fans can buy licensed fan gear, jerseys, lifestyle and streetwear products, headwear, and hardgoods; collect physical and digital trading cards, sports memorabilia, and other digital assets; and bet as the company builds its Sportsbook and iGaming platform. Fanatics has an established database of over 100 million global sports fans; a global partner network with approximately 900 sports properties, including major national and international professional sports leagues, players associations, teams, colleges, college conferences and retail partners, 2,500 athletes and celebrities, and 200 exclusive athletes; and over 2,000 retail locations, including its Lids retail stores. Our more than 22,000 employees are committed to relentlessly enhancing the fan experience and delighting sports fans globally.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Company&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Fanatics Collect is a global product and technology group dedicated to revolutionizing the world of collectibles. Every single day our team of experienced product leaders, engineers, and operators obsesses over how to create the ultimate collector experience with our products: Topps.com, the direct to consumer ecommerce platform of the Topps brand, Fanatics Collect, the most trusted and dynamic collector focused marketplace, and our collector focused live shopping platforms, Fanatics Live and Voggt.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have the unique advantage of being backed by Fanatics - the world’s largest sports merchandiser, with more than 900 global sports relationships, 90+ million reachable fans, and exclusive licensing deals with the MLB, NFL, and NBA among many others - but we’re a nimble, ambitious team building products from the ground up.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you&#39;re passionate about building world class products and share our love for sports fans and collectors, Fanatics Collect offers an exciting opportunity to be part of a dynamic team creating the future of collecting.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Fanatics Collect is seeking a Senior Manager, Collector Loyalty to lead the go-to-market strategy and collector experience for Fanatics ONE and FanCash across Fanatics Live, Fanatics Collect, and Topps. This role sits at the intersection of Growth, Product, Marketing, and Analytics, translating enterprise loyalty initiatives into clear, scalable programs that drive adoption, engagement, retention, and long-term customer value.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;br&gt;The ideal candidate combines strategic thinking with operational excellence and possesses a deep understanding of loyalty ecosystems, customer journeys, and go-to-market execution. You will partner across multiple business units to ensure Fanatics ONE delivers a cohesive, differentiated, and compelling experience for collectors while supporting measurable business outcomes.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and execute loyalty go-to-market strategies for Fanatics ONE and FanCash across Fanatics Live, Fanatics Collect, and Topps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own all loyalty go-to-market campaigns and initiatives across TLC (Topps, Fanatics Live, and Fanatics Collect), serving as the central point of accountability from strategy through execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate enterprise loyalty objectives into actionable launch plans, messaging frameworks, and execution roadmaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure the loyalty program is financially viable for TLC, balancing compelling collector value with sustainable program economics and measurable return.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish a clear, robust, and easy-to-communicate value proposition for what loyalty means to TLC and the Hobby — one that resonates with both new and existing collectors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define customer-facing value propositions and positioning for loyalty products, benefits, and rewards programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive cross-functional coordination across Growth, CRM, Product, Analytics, Brand, and Operations teams to support loyalty initiatives and launches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the annual loyalty marketing calendar, aligning campaigns with key commercial moments, product launches, and collector behaviors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with CRM and Lifecycle Marketing teams to deliver integrated loyalty experiences across email, push, onsite, in-product, and live commerce channels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with Product and Engineering teams to support loyalty feature launches, adoption initiatives, and customer education efforts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the international adaptation of loyalty, tailoring program design, positioning, and rollout to local markets and collector communities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and analyze performance across key metrics including adoption, engagement, retention, purchase frequency, and FanCash utilization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver ongoing reporting on ROI of loyalty spend, giving leadership clear, recurring visibility into program cost, return, and efficiency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Analytics and Data Science teams to identify insights, optimize campaigns, and improve loyalty program performance through experimentation and testing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with Brand and Creative teams to develop compelling loyalty messaging, storytelling, and campaign assets that resonate with fans and collectors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Marketing, Communications, Business, or a related field.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of experience in loyalty marketing, product marketing, lifecycle marketing, growth marketing, or go-to-market roles within e-commerce, marketplaces, consumer technology, media, or related industries.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience launching and scaling loyalty, rewards, retention, or membership programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of customer lifecycle marketing, segmentation, personalization, and engagement strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering closely with Product and Engineering teams to drive adoption of customer-facing features and experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with analytics platforms, experimentation frameworks, and customer behavior tools such as Amplitude, Looker, Tableau, or similar platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical mindset with the ability to interpret performance data, develop insights, and make data-driven recommendations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional written and verbal communication skills with the ability to influence stakeholders across all organizational levels.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly organized project manager capable of managing multiple initiatives simultaneously in a fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to build strong cross-functional relationships and drive alignment without direct authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for sports, fandom, collectibles, loyalty programs, and consumer engagement experiences preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s1&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Ensure your Fanatics job offer is legitimate and don’t fall victim to fraud.&amp;nbsp; Fanatics never seeks payment from job applicants. Feel free to ask your recruiter for a phone call or other type of communication for interview, and ensure your communication is coming from a Fanatics email address (including @collectfanatics.com).&amp;nbsp; For added security, where possible, apply through our company website at&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.fanaticsinc.com/careers&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s2&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;www.fanaticsinc.com/careers&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The salary range represents base pay only and does not include short-term or long-term incentive compensation. &amp;nbsp;This salary range is specific to New York City and may not be applicable to other locations. &amp;nbsp;When determining base pay, as part of a final compensation package, we consider several factors such as location, experience, qualifications, and training. For information about our benefits, please visit&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://benefitsatfanatics.com/&quot;&gt;https://benefitsatfanatics.com/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;NYC Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$150,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$190,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By submitting your application, you agree to our terms of service and acknowledge you have read our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://static1.squarespace.com/static/5ff494b9931735466ce28d5b/t/69de53bde2c02c25e9c38758/1776178110037/Candidate+Privacy+Policy+April+2026.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Candidate Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Fanatics will never ask candidates for money, banking information, or other sensitive personal information as part of the interview process. If you receive a suspicious message claiming to be from Fanatics recruiting, please do not respond and report it&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:recruiting-fraud@fanaticsinc.com&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;here&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 class=&quot;job-details__description-header text-color-secondary font-family-secondary&quot; data-bind=&quot;i18n: &#39;job-details.employer-description-title&#39;&quot;&gt;About Us&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;job-details__description-content basic-formatter&quot; data-bind=&quot;html: pageData().job.corporateDescription&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Fanatics is building a leading global digital sports platform. We ignite the passions of global sports fans and maximize the presence and reach for our hundreds of sports partners globally by offering products and services across Fanatics Commerce, Fanatics Collectibles, and Fanatics Betting &amp;amp; Gaming, allowing sports fans to Buy, Collect, and Bet. Through the Fanatics platform, sports fans can buy licensed fan gear, jerseys, lifestyle and streetwear products, headwear, and hardgoods; collect physical and digital trading cards, sports memorabilia, and other digital assets; and bet as the company builds its Sportsbook and iGaming platform. Fanatics has an established database of over 100 million global sports fans; a global partner network with approximately 900 sports properties, including major national and international professional sports leagues, players associations, teams, colleges, college conferences and retail partners, 2,500 athletes and celebrities, and 200 exclusive athletes; and over 2,000 retail locations, including its Lids retail stores. Our more than 22,000 employees are committed to relentlessly enhancing the fan experience and delighting sports fans globally.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Company&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fanatics Collectibles is a new company operating at the intersection of collectibles, culture, and technology. Backed by world-class investors, operators, and sports &amp;amp; entertainment partners, we are building the global leader in next-generation collectibles. As part of the broader Fanatics ecosystem, we leverage a digital sports platform that spans over 900 sports properties and engages more than 81 million fans. Together, we are reimagining every part of the collectibles experience for fans, partners, and creators.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;JDBody&quot;&gt;We&#39;re looking for a Senior Manager, Commercial Programming to lead the strategy and operating model for how Fanatics Collect turns moments across sports, culture, collectibles, and our product ecosystem into scaled commercial programming. This leader will build and own the Commercial Programming function, establishing the strategy, priorities, operating rhythms, and performance framework that connect our commercial objectives with compelling entertainment experiences.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;JDBody&quot;&gt;Today, much of the activity on our platform is driven by product releases. This role will broaden that model by building an integrated programming portfolio spanning product launches, the sports calendar, cultural and seasonal moments, seller-led programming, talent and creator opportunities, and original Fanatics Collect programming. The Senior Manager will determine where we invest, establish priorities across opportunities, lead cross-functional execution, and build the team and capabilities required to deliver the strategy at scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;SectionHeading&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;BulletText&quot;&gt;Own the Commercial Programming strategy, operating plan, and integrated roadmap across product releases, sports and cultural moments, seasonal opportunities, seller-led programming, recurring franchises, and original Fanatics Collect programming.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;BulletText&quot;&gt;Establish annual and quarterly programming priorities, investment principles, KPIs, and decision frameworks based on commercial objectives, customer behavior, seller opportunities, platform capabilities, and the sports and cultural calendar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;BulletText&quot;&gt;Translate broader Commercial strategy into actionable programming objectives and make prioritization, budget, and resource-allocation decisions across competing opportunities and short lead-time business needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;BulletText&quot;&gt;Lead the development of scalable programming concepts and original franchises involving creators, athletes, teams, leagues, sellers, and other talent, including new live selling formats that combine compelling entertainment experiences with strong commercial outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;BulletText&quot;&gt;Establish scalable programming models, processes, and standards that enable successful concepts to be repeated across categories, sellers, sports, and customer segments; create mechanisms to test new concepts, measure results, and scale winning formats.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;BulletText&quot;&gt;Serve as the senior Commercial Programming partner across Account Management, Paid, Lifecycle, Influencer, Product, and other functions, establishing clear operating rhythms, ownership models, and decision-making processes from concept through execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;BulletText&quot;&gt;Partner with Product leadership to align programming strategy with platform capabilities and identify new product capabilities that can unlock differentiated commercial, entertainment, and customer experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;BulletText&quot;&gt;Partner with Account Management leadership to define the seller programming strategy, including seller participation in major platform moments and opportunities to evolve seller streams into stronger entertainment experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;BulletText&quot;&gt;Own performance management for the programming portfolio, using commercial and customer KPIs to identify opportunities, diagnose gaps, and inform changes to strategy, investment, and execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;BulletText&quot;&gt;Build, lead, and develop a high-performing Commercial Programming team, establishing clear roles, workflows, performance expectations, and resource plans while developing expertise across commercial strategy, programming, live selling, content, and performance analysis.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;SectionHeading&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;text-decoration: underline;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;BulletText&quot;&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Business, Marketing, Media, Communications, or a related field preferred, or equivalent relevant professional experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;BulletText&quot;&gt;7+ years of relevant experience across commercial or growth marketing, content or editorial programming, live commerce, marketplace businesses, media and entertainment, or related fields, including meaningful experience leading teams or complex multidisciplinary programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;BulletText&quot;&gt;Demonstrated success developing and implementing programming, commercial, content, or growth strategies tied to measurable business and customer outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;BulletText&quot;&gt;Experience managing and developing professional employees, building effective team operating models, and allocating resources across a complex portfolio of priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;BulletText&quot;&gt;Deep understanding of live selling ecosystems and the relationship between content quality, seller behavior, audience engagement, product experience, and commercial performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;BulletText&quot;&gt;Demonstrated ability to translate broad business objectives into clear strategies, priorities, operating plans, processes, and measurable programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;BulletText&quot;&gt;Strong commercial judgment, analytical capabilities, and experience defining KPIs, evaluating portfolio performance, and using data to make prioritization, investment, and resource-allocation decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;BulletText&quot;&gt;Proven ability to lead complex cross-functional initiatives and influence senior stakeholders across teams with different objectives, priorities, and dependencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;BulletText&quot;&gt;Strong executive communication, stakeholder management, and leadership skills, with the ability to operate effectively in a fast-paced, highly collaborative environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li class=&quot;BulletText&quot;&gt;Experience working with creators, livestreamers, athletes, teams, leagues, or on-camera talent is strongly preferred; deep knowledge of the collecting, breaking, sports, and entertainment ecosystems is a significant advantage.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
