&lt;p&gt;By submitting your application, you agree to our terms of service and acknowledge you have read our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://static1.squarespace.com/static/5ff494b9931735466ce28d5b/t/69de53bde2c02c25e9c38758/1776178110037/Candidate+Privacy+Policy+April+2026.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Candidate Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Fanatics will never ask candidates for money, banking information, or other sensitive personal information as part of the interview process. If you receive a suspicious message claiming to be from Fanatics recruiting, please do not respond and report it&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:recruiting-fraud@fanaticsinc.com&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;here&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 class=&quot;job-details__description-header text-color-secondary font-family-secondary&quot; data-bind=&quot;i18n: &#39;job-details.employer-description-title&#39;&quot;&gt;About Us&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;job-details__description-content basic-formatter&quot; data-bind=&quot;html: pageData().job.corporateDescription&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Fanatics is building a leading global digital sports platform. We ignite the passions of global sports fans and maximize the presence and reach for our hundreds of sports partners globally by offering products and services across Fanatics Commerce, Fanatics Collectibles, and Fanatics Betting &amp;amp; Gaming, allowing sports fans to Buy, Collect, and Bet. Through the Fanatics platform, sports fans can buy licensed fan gear, jerseys, lifestyle and streetwear products, headwear, and hardgoods; collect physical and digital trading cards, sports memorabilia, and other digital assets; and bet as the company builds its Sportsbook and iGaming platform. Fanatics has an established database of over 100 million global sports fans; a global partner network with approximately 900 sports properties, including major national and international professional sports leagues, players associations, teams, colleges, college conferences and retail partners, 2,500 athletes and celebrities, and 200 exclusive athletes; and over 2,000 retail locations, including its Lids retail stores. Our more than 22,000 employees are committed to relentlessly enhancing the fan experience and delighting sports fans globally.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Company&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fanatics Collectibles is a new company operating at the intersection of collectibles, culture, and technology. Backed by world-class investors, operators, and sports &amp;amp; entertainment partners, we are building the global leader in next-generation collectibles. As part of the broader Fanatics ecosystem, we leverage a digital sports platform that spans over 900 sports properties and engages more than 81 million fans. Together, we are reimagining every part of the collectibles experience for fans, partners, and creators.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fanatics Collectibles is building trusted digital experiences where collectors can discover, engage, buy, and sell across Fanatics Live and Fanatics Collect Marketplace. We are seeking a Senior Product Manager to lead the development of Trust &amp;amp; Safety technology and product capabilities that help protect customers, sellers, creators, and the integrity of our platforms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will define product strategy and roadmap for Trust &amp;amp; Safety technology spanning Live and Marketplace. You will translate customer, business, operational, and risk needs into scalable product solutions and lead cross-functional teams from discovery through launch and optimization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will work closely with engineering, design, analytics, Customer Experience, Trust &amp;amp; Safety, Fraud Prevention, Payments, Financial Operations, and product teams across Live and Marketplace. Your work will balance creating low-friction experiences for trusted users with building the technology needed to prevent, detect, investigate, and respond to harmful, fraudulent, abusive, or otherwise high-risk activity.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As part of Fanatics Collectibles’ continued global growth, we are establishing a new technology hub in Mexico City focused on operational excellence, platform scalability, trust, and customer experience. This team will build scalable systems and operational tooling that support millions of users and transactions globally.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What You’ll Do&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and evolve the product strategy and roadmap for Trust &amp;amp; Safety technology across Fanatics Live and Fanatics Collect Marketplace, including shared platform capabilities, customer-facing experiences, and internal operational tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with product teams across Live and Marketplace to identify where Trust &amp;amp; Safety capabilities should be embedded into customer, seller, creator, and transaction experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Trust &amp;amp; Safety, Fraud Prevention, CX, Payments, engineering, data, and operations teams to identify emerging risks and translate them into scalable product and technology solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop capabilities that help prevent, detect, investigate, and resolve harmful, fraudulent, abusive, or otherwise high-risk activity while minimizing unnecessary friction for trusted users.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build shared Trust &amp;amp; Safety capabilities that can support multiple product experiences while accounting for the distinct needs of livestream commerce and marketplace transactions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead development of internal tools and workflows that enable Trust &amp;amp; Safety and operational teams to review activity, investigate cases, manage queues and customer exceptions, and take appropriate action efficiently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify product opportunities through customer research, behavioral data, risk signals, operational insights, incident trends, and partnership with internal teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate complex Trust &amp;amp; Safety and operational workflows into clear product requirements, prioritized user stories, and intuitive customer and internal experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with engineering and design throughout discovery, development, launch, and iteration, including defining requirements for platform capabilities, integrations, and operational tooling.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define success measures and use data to evaluate customer trust, platform integrity, operational efficiency, user friction, and the effectiveness of Trust &amp;amp; Safety interventions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Balance customer and creator experience, commercial priorities, risk mitigation, operational requirements, and technical constraints when making product and roadmap decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Anticipate dependencies across identity, account integrity, payments, transactions, seller and creator experiences, fraud prevention, customer support, data, and other platform capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop launch plans, align stakeholders, assess operational and risk readiness, and communicate product decisions, tradeoffs, and results to senior leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor platform performance and emerging patterns after launch and establish a disciplined approach to experimentation, measurement, and iteration.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to a broader Trust &amp;amp; Safety technology strategy that enables Fanatics Collectibles to scale trusted customer and commerce experiences globally.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;What We’re Looking For&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Five or more years of product management experience building and scaling customer-facing, platform, or operational technology products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ownership of complex products or platforms from strategy and discovery through launch and ongoing optimization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience partnering with engineering teams to deliver technically complex products, platforms, or internal tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills and experience using customer insights, product data, operational metrics, and risk signals to guide decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to translate ambiguous customer, business, operational, and risk problems into clear product priorities and executable plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of digital platform or commerce dynamics and the relationship between customer experience, trust, risk, and business performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to think systematically about product abuse and unintended behaviors, including how bad actors may exploit product features, interactions, or workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience influencing across multiple product and functional teams and aligning stakeholders with different objectives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Clear written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to communicate complex product and risk tradeoffs to senior leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong product judgment, attention to detail, and a bias toward delivering measurable customer and business outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Preferred Qualifications&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience building Trust &amp;amp; Safety, fraud prevention, risk, identity, account integrity, payments, or platform integrity products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with e-commerce, marketplaces, livestreaming, social/community products, fintech, auctions, or other transaction-oriented platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with Trust &amp;amp; Safety technology patterns such as detection and decisioning systems, user reporting, case management, review queues, enforcement workflows, appeals, and risk signals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing tools that help Trust &amp;amp; Safety, fraud, CX, or operations teams investigate and resolve cases at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with data science, machine learning, rules-based systems, or other automated approaches to identifying and mitigating risky behavior.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with real-time or time-sensitive product experiences, particularly livestreaming, bidding, payments, chat, notifications, or live events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience defining metrics that balance risk reduction and operational effectiveness with customer experience and product growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interest in trading cards, collectibles, livestream commerce, marketplaces, or collector communities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;How You’ll Make an Impact&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will help build the technology foundation that enables Fanatics Live and Fanatics Collect Marketplace to grow as trusted platforms. Your work will give customers, sellers, and creators greater confidence when they engage and transact while providing Fanatics teams with scalable technology to identify risk, protect users, and operate safely and efficiently.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By developing capabilities that can be shared across Live and Marketplace, you will help Fanatics Collectibles address today’s Trust &amp;amp; Safety needs while establishing a foundation that can evolve as our products, communities, and global customer base grow.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s1&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Ensure your Fanatics job offer is legitimate and don’t fall victim to fraud.&amp;nbsp; Fanatics never seeks payment from job applicants.&amp;nbsp;Feel free to ask your recruiter for a phone call or other type of communication for interview, and ensure your communication is coming from a Fanatics email address (including @collectfanatics.com).&amp;nbsp; For added security, where possible, apply through our company website at&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.fanaticsinc.com/careers&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s2&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;www.fanaticsinc.com/careers&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By submitting your application, you agree to our terms of service and acknowledge you have read our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://static1.squarespace.com/static/5ff494b9931735466ce28d5b/t/69de53bde2c02c25e9c38758/1776178110037/Candidate+Privacy+Policy+April+2026.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Candidate Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
