&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 class=&quot;job-details__description-header text-color-secondary font-family-secondary&quot; data-bind=&quot;i18n: &#39;job-details.employer-description-title&#39;&quot;&gt;About Us&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;job-details__description-content basic-formatter&quot; data-bind=&quot;html: pageData().job.corporateDescription&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Fanatics is building a leading global digital sports platform. We ignite the passions of global sports fans and maximize the presence and reach for our hundreds of sports partners globally by offering products and services across Fanatics Commerce, Fanatics Collectibles, and Fanatics Betting &amp;amp; Gaming, allowing sports fans to Buy, Collect, and Bet. Through the Fanatics platform, sports fans can buy licensed fan gear, jerseys, lifestyle and streetwear products, headwear, and hardgoods; collect physical and digital trading cards, sports memorabilia, and other digital assets; and bet as the company builds its Sportsbook and iGaming platform. Fanatics has an established database of over 100 million global sports fans; a global partner network with approximately 900 sports properties, including major national and international professional sports leagues, players associations, teams, colleges, college conferences and retail partners, 2,500 athletes and celebrities, and 200 exclusive athletes; and over 2,000 retail locations, including its Lids retail stores. Our more than 22,000 employees are committed to relentlessly enhancing the fan experience and delighting sports fans globally.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Company Background&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Topps, a legendary name in trading cards and collectibles, is a digital-first division within Fanatics. At Fanatics Collectibles, we&#39;re reimagining the collector experience with cutting-edge digital platforms across Topps.com, the Fanatics Collect marketplace, and Fanatics Live. Our growth and lifecycle marketing runs on a modern MarTech stack — and we need an engineer to own it.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Senior Software Engineer, Event Data Platform (Growth)&lt;/strong&gt; to own our event stream from Segment through every downstream destination — Braze, Amplitude, Snowflake, AppsFlyer, and ad platforms. You will be the technical owner of how event data is governed, transformed, routed, and consumed once it reaches our CDP: schemas, identity, audiences, destination configuration, and delivery reliability all belong to you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Upstream of Segment, you will partner with engineers across web, mobile, and backend to define event contracts, review instrumentation, and ensure what lands in Segment is correct, complete, and usable downstream. This is not a &quot;keep the lights on&quot; integration role. Our eventing and attribution infrastructure spans multiple products, and we need a hands-on owner who can drive it toward a single, governed source of truth while supporting high-velocity growth experimentation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Event Stream Ownership (Segment → Downstream): Own the event pipeline from Segment through all downstream MarTech destinations — Braze, Amplitude, Snowflake, AppsFlyer, and ad platforms. Own destination configuration, transformations, audience sync, and delivery reliability. Contribute to the evolution toward Segment as the single source of truth, including facade/proxy service patterns that decouple product code from destination-specific logic.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Upstream Partnership &amp;amp; Event Contracts: Work closely with product and data engineering teams across Topps, Collect, and Live to influence how events arrive in Segment. Define event contracts and schema standards, review instrumentation changes, and validate that payloads emitted by web, mobile, and backend systems are correct and complete before they enter the pipeline.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Identity Resolution: Own the identity model within Segment and downstream destinations — ensuring users are consistently and correctly resolved across event sources so that audiences, attribution, and lifecycle messaging reach the right person.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Lifecycle &amp;amp; Engagement Integrations: Implement and maintain Braze integrations, including audience sync, catalog/data feeds, and event-triggered messaging. Validate triggers, rendering, and data flows. Partner with lifecycle marketing to translate campaign requirements into reliable implementations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Attribution &amp;amp; Measurement: Own AppsFlyer configuration and mobile attribution, UTM and web attribution integrity, and the downstream routing that lets us measure which channels drive acquisition.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Data Governance &amp;amp; Cost Control: Establish event schema standards, naming conventions, and QA gates. Audit and manage destination configuration, event volume, and platform spend across the stack.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- 5+ years of software engineering experience, with a focus on integrating third-party platforms and SDKs within complex ecosystems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Strong SQL — able to independently validate data end to end, from raw event streams to warehouse tables.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Deep, hands-on experience with at least 2–3 of: Segment (or another CDP such as mParticle), Braze (or Iterable/Klaviyo/SFMC), Amplitude, Snowflake, AppsFlyer (or another MMP). Direct experience with competitor tools in each category counts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Working knowledge of web and/or mobile client technologies (React/NextJS, Swift, or Kotlin) — enough to review instrumentation, understand SDK behavior within application lifecycles, and partner credibly with product engineers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Expertise in event-driven architecture, data instrumentation, and payload validation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Proven track record troubleshooting distributed systems and ensuring data integrity across multiple platforms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Exceptional communication skills — able to translate marketing and growth requirements into technical specifications, influence engineering teams you don&#39;t manage, and push back with data when requirements conflict with sound architecture.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 10pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desired Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Experience designing or operating an event facade/proxy service in front of a CDP.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- CDP governance at scale, including event volume and cost optimization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Identity resolution across multiple user ID systems (e.g., auth IDs, commerce platform IDs, device IDs).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Experience in e-commerce or gaming, where real-time engagement and high-volume event flows are critical.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- A/B testing and experimentation platform experience.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Cross-functional collaboration experience spanning Product, Marketing, and Engineering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Ensure your Fanatics job offer is legitimate and don’t fall victim to fraud.&amp;nbsp; Fanatics never seeks payment from job applicants. Feel free to ask your recruiter for a phone call or other type of communication for interview, and ensure your communication is coming from a Fanatics email address (including @collectfanatics.com).&amp;nbsp; For added security, where possible, apply through our company website at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.fanaticsinc.com/careers&quot;&gt;www.fanaticsinc.com/careers&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The salary range represents base pay only and does not include short-term or long-term incentive compensation. &amp;nbsp;This salary range is specific to New York City and may not be applicable to other locations. &amp;nbsp;When determining base pay, as part of a final compensation package, we consider several factors such as location, experience, qualifications, and training. For information about our benefits, please visit&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://benefitsatfanatics.com/&quot;&gt;https://benefitsatfanatics.com/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;NYC Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$160,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$200,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By submitting your application, you agree to our terms of service and acknowledge you have read our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://static1.squarespace.com/static/5ff494b9931735466ce28d5b/t/69de53bde2c02c25e9c38758/1776178110037/Candidate+Privacy+Policy+April+2026.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Candidate Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Fanatics will never ask candidates for money, banking information, or other sensitive personal information as part of the interview process. If you receive a suspicious message claiming to be from Fanatics recruiting, please do not respond and report it&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:recruiting-fraud@fanaticsinc.com&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;here&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

