&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Company&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Fanatics Collectibles is a new company operating at the intersection of collectibles, culture, and technology. Backed by world-class investors, operators, and sports &amp;amp; entertainment partners, we are building the global leader in next-generation collectibles. As part of the broader Fanatics ecosystem, we leverage a digital sports platform that spans over 900 sports properties and engages more than 81 million fans. Together, we are reimagining every part of the collectibles experience for fans, partners, and creators.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Fanatics Collectibles is building the global infrastructure to support the fastest-growing collectibles business in the world. We are looking for a Manager or Senior Manager of International Supply Chain Strategy to design and stand up end-to-end supply chain capabilities for new international markets—often from zero.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;This role will partner closely with Commercial, Drops, Product, Technology, Finance, Legal, and Operations teams to build scalable, compliant product flows that support highly anticipated launches, time-sensitive drops, and premium collector experiences. You will help determine how trading cards, sealed product, and other collectibles move from production to collectors across new geographies—at speed, at scale, and in compliance with complex international customs and import requirements.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;This is a highly visible role for someone who thrives in ambiguity, moves quickly, and enjoys building new supply chain models to support hyper growth.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Zero-to-One Market &amp;amp; Product Flow Design&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Design end-to-end international supply chain models to support new Fanatics Collectibles market launches&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Build product flows from the ground up, including inbound logistics, inventory positioning, fulfillment, and returns&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Partner with Commercial and Drops teams to translate product strategies, launch calendars, and growth targets into executable supply chain plans&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Balance speed, cost, service, scalability, and risk to support high-velocity launches and sustained growth&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Inbound &amp;amp; Global Product Flows&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Define inbound transportation strategies for trading cards and collectibles, including factory-to-market flows, cross-border movement, and regional distribution&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Design inbound flows that navigate complex customs clearance, regulatory requirements, and market-specific import processes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Develop processes to support launch-based inbound spikes, limited runs, and demand surges tied to drops&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Partner with Finance and Commercial teams to model landed cost, margin impact, and working capital implications&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Develop contingency plans for customs delays, inspections, or regulatory changes that could impact launch timing or inventory availability&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;International Trade, Customs &amp;amp; Regulatory Strategy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Design cross-border supply chain strategies that comply with country-specific customs, import, and regulatory requirements for collectibles&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Partner with Legal, Tax, Finance, and external advisors to determine optimal import structures, entity usage, and compliance approaches for new markets&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Define customs clearance strategies, documentation requirements, and broker models to support high-speed launches and ongoing operations&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Evaluate duties, taxes, fees, and other trade costs and incorporate them into landed cost, pricing, and margin models&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Anticipate and mitigate customs-related risks (holds, delays, inspections, seizures) that could impact customer experience or business performance&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Build repeatable playbooks for entering new countries while accounting for local regulatory nuances&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Order Management &amp;amp; Systems Enablement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Partner with Technology teams to define order management system (OMS) requirements that support collectibles-specific needs, including drops, allocations, customer promise logic, and fraud controls&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Ensure inventory visibility, order routing, and fulfillment logic align with market-specific constraints and customer expectations&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Identify system or process gaps that could limit international growth and drive solutions through tooling, configuration, or new capabilities&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Fulfillment &amp;amp; Partner Ecosystem Strategy&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Identify, evaluate, and onboard international fulfillment and logistics partners capable of handling high-value collectibles&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Design fulfillment models that support launch-day volume spikes, rapid order turnaround, and premium packaging requirements&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Lead RFPs, partner selection, and business case development for new markets and capacity expansions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Define SLAs, performance metrics, and escalation models to protect customer experience during peak demand&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Evaluate partners based on their ability to support local customs, regulatory, and compliance requirements&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Returns, Exceptions &amp;amp; Collector Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Design returns, replacements, and exception-handling processes appropriate for collectibles, including damaged product, lost shipments, missing hits, and fraud scenarios&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Partner with Customer Service and Commercial teams to ensure supply chain decisions protect collector trust and brand reputation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Develop market-specific solutions for customer issues, regulatory requirements, and edge cases&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Leadership &amp;amp; Growth Enablement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Serve as the supply chain strategy lead for international expansion within Fanatics Collectibles&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Act as a connective tissue between Commercial, Product, Technology, Finance, Legal, and Global Operations teams&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Lead pilots, launch readiness activities, and post-launch retrospectives&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Identify opportunities to standardize, scale, and industrialize solutions as markets mature&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;6–10+ years of experience in supply chain strategy, operations, logistics, or management consulting (level dependent)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Experience building or scaling supply chains in high-growth, launch-driven environments&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Strong understanding of inbound logistics, fulfillment operations, order management, and reverse logistics&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Proven ability to work cross-functionally and influence senior stakeholders without direct authority&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Strong analytical and financial modeling skills, including cost-to-serve and scenario modeling&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Comfortable operating in fast-paced, ambiguous environments with incomplete data&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Experience supporting international expansion and cross-border supply chains&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Exposure to customs, import/export compliance, or trade advisory work (hands-on expertise not required)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Experience working with international 3PLs, freight forwarders, and customs brokers&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Experience in collectibles, e-commerce, DTC, marketplaces, or premium consumer goods&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Familiarity with HS classification, valuation considerations, and country-specific import processes&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;MBA or advanced degree a plus&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s1&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Ensure your Fanatics job offer is legitimate and don’t fall victim to fraud.&amp;nbsp; Fanatics never seeks payment from job applicants.&amp;nbsp;Feel free to ask your recruiter for a phone call or other type of communication for interview, and ensure your communication is coming from a Fanatics email address (including @collectfanatics.com).&amp;nbsp; For added security, where possible, apply through our company website at&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.fanaticsinc.com/careers&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s2&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;www.fanaticsinc.com/careers&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The salary range represents base pay only and does not include short-term or long-term incentive compensation. &amp;nbsp;This salary range is specific to New York City and may not be applicable to other locations. &amp;nbsp;When determining base pay, as part of a final compensation package, we consider several factors such as location, experience, qualifications, and training. For information about our benefits, please visit&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://benefitsatfanatics.com/&quot;&gt;https://benefitsatfanatics.com/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;NYC Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$170,000&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$196,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By submitting your application, you agree to our terms of service and acknowledge you have read our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://static1.squarespace.com/static/5ff494b9931735466ce28d5b/t/69de53bde2c02c25e9c38758/1776178110037/Candidate+Privacy+Policy+April+2026.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Candidate Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Fanatics will never ask candidates for money, banking information, or other sensitive personal information as part of the interview process. If you receive a suspicious message claiming to be from Fanatics recruiting, please do not respond and report it&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:recruiting-fraud@fanaticsinc.com&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;here&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 class=&quot;job-details__description-header text-color-secondary font-family-secondary&quot; data-bind=&quot;i18n: &#39;job-details.employer-description-title&#39;&quot;&gt;About Us&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;job-details__description-content basic-formatter&quot; data-bind=&quot;html: pageData().job.corporateDescription&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Fanatics is building a leading global digital sports platform. We ignite the passions of global sports fans and maximize the presence and reach for our hundreds of sports partners globally by offering products and services across Fanatics Commerce, Fanatics Collectibles, and Fanatics Betting &amp;amp; Gaming, allowing sports fans to Buy, Collect, and Bet. Through the Fanatics platform, sports fans can buy licensed fan gear, jerseys, lifestyle and streetwear products, headwear, and hardgoods; collect physical and digital trading cards, sports memorabilia, and other digital assets; and bet as the company builds its Sportsbook and iGaming platform. Fanatics has an established database of over 100 million global sports fans; a global partner network with approximately 900 sports properties, including major national and international professional sports leagues, players associations, teams, colleges, college conferences and retail partners, 2,500 athletes and celebrities, and 200 exclusive athletes; and over 2,000 retail locations, including its Lids retail stores. Our more than 22,000 employees are committed to relentlessly enhancing the fan experience and delighting sports fans globally.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reports to&lt;/strong&gt;: Sr. Director, Strategic Finance&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location&lt;/strong&gt;: NYC&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Other&lt;/strong&gt;: Full Time In-Office Position; periodic travel to Portland, Oregon required, typically a few times per quarter.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Company&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fanatics Collect is a global product and technology group dedicated to revolutionizing the world of collectibles. Every single day our team of experienced product leaders, engineers, and operators obsesses over how to create the ultimate collector experience with our products: Topps.com, the direct to consumer ecommerce platform of the Topps brand, Fanatics Collect, the most trusted and dynamic collector focused marketplace, and our collector focused live shopping platforms, Fanatics Live and Voggt.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We have the unique advantage of being backed by Fanatics - the world’s largest sports merchandiser, with more than 900 global sports relationships, 90+ million reachable fans, and exclusive licensing deals with the MLB, NFL, and NBA among many others - but we’re a nimble, ambitious team building products from the ground up.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you&#39;re passionate about building world class products and share our love for sports fans and collectors, Fanatics Collect offers an exciting opportunity to be part of a dynamic team creating the future of collecting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Sr. Manager, Strategic Finance – Business Operations is the embedded finance leader for&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fanatics Collect’s Vault Operations, Customer Service, Shipping, Payment Processing, Trust &amp;amp; Safety, and People organizations. This role partners closely with FP&amp;amp;A and functional leaders on operational forecasting and reporting, drives improvements in efficiency, unit economics, and customer experience, and owns workforce and headcount financial planning, people-cost budgets, and financial support for the People team.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is designed for a finance leader who combines rigorous analytical thinking with deep operational curiosity and a bias for action. The ideal candidate is equally comfortable building sophisticated financial models, working directly with teams on the Vault floor to understand processes and cost drivers, and advising senior leaders on operational improvements and workforce investments.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the dedicated finance partner to operational and People leaders, developing deep knowledge of each function’s operating model, cost structure, vendor relationships, process flows, and key performance drivers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and lead opportunities to improve unit economics across the business, including cost per shipment, authentication, customer contact, and transaction processed, as well as payment processing fees, fraud rates, and loss rates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own business cases, financial modeling, implementation support, and post-implementation performance tracking for strategic initiatives including shipping carrier negotiations, Vault cost optimization, customer service staffing and automation, payments routing, and fraud mitigation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with operating leaders to translate financial and operational analysis into concrete actions, establish measurable targets, and create accountability for delivering financial and operational outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with FP&amp;amp;A on annual budgets, forecasts, and ongoing performance management across the operations portfolio, providing detailed cost-driver analysis and operational judgment to improve forecast accuracy and proactively identify risks and opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own org-wide headcount and people-cost budgets, forecasts, and long-range financial plans, maintaining detailed position-level models covering compensation, benefits, payroll taxes, equity expense, contractors, hiring, attrition, and compensation changes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with People and business leaders on workforce planning, helping evaluate hiring plans, organizational investments, compensation decisions, and tradeoffs while ensuring workforce plans align with the company’s financial and strategic priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop scalable reporting, dashboards, and performance metrics that give leaders clear visibility into operational efficiency, workforce costs, unit economics, and progress against financial targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Synthesize complex financial and operational data into clear insights and recommendations for senior leadership, helping drive faster, more informed decisions across the organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree in Finance, Accounting, Economics, Business, or a related quantitative field; MBA or other relevant advanced degree preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of progressive experience in strategic finance, FP&amp;amp;A, corporate finance, investment banking, consulting, business operations, or a related analytical role, including experience partnering directly with senior business leaders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong financial modeling and analytical capabilities, with demonstrated experience building detailed operating models, budgets, forecasts, business cases, and scenario analyses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting operational functions and analyzing unit economics, cost drivers, productivity, vendor economics, and process efficiency; experience with logistics, payments, customer service, fraud, marketplace, ecommerce, or fulfillment operations is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience with headcount planning, workforce modeling, compensation and people-cost forecasting, or financial partnership with People/HR organizations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advanced proficiency in Excel and/or Google Sheets and experience working with financial planning, ERP, BI, and data visualization tools; ability to work comfortably with large and complex datasets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong business judgment and ability to move beyond reporting results to identify underlying drivers, develop recommendations, and influence operational decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communication and stakeholder-management skills, with the ability to translate complex analysis into concise, actionable insights for financial, operational, People, and executive audiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly collaborative, intellectually curious, and comfortable operating with ambiguity in a fast-paced, high-growth environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s1&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Ensure your Fanatics job offer is legitimate and don’t fall victim to fraud.&amp;nbsp; Fanatics never seeks payment from job applicants. Feel free to ask your recruiter for a phone call or other type of communication for interview, and ensure your communication is coming from a Fanatics email address (including @collectfanatics.com).&amp;nbsp; For added security, where possible, apply through our company website at &lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.fanaticsinc.com/careers&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s2&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;www.fanaticsinc.com/careers&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-pay-transparency&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-input&quot;&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;description&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;The salary range represents base pay only and does not include short-term or long-term incentive compensation. &amp;nbsp;This salary range is specific to New York City and may not be applicable to other locations. &amp;nbsp;When determining base pay, as part of a final compensation package, we consider several factors such as location, experience, qualifications, and training. For information about our benefits, please visit&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://benefitsatfanatics.com/&quot;&gt;https://benefitsatfanatics.com/&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;title&quot;&gt;NYC Salary Range&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;pay-range&quot;&gt;&lt;span&gt;$168,750&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;divider&quot;&gt;&amp;mdash;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span&gt;$210,000 USD&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By submitting your application, you agree to our terms of service and acknowledge you have read our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://static1.squarespace.com/static/5ff494b9931735466ce28d5b/t/69de53bde2c02c25e9c38758/1776178110037/Candidate+Privacy+Policy+April+2026.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Candidate Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Fanatics will never ask candidates for money, banking information, or other sensitive personal information as part of the interview process. If you receive a suspicious message claiming to be from Fanatics recruiting, please do not respond and report it&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:recruiting-fraud@fanaticsinc.com&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;here&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 class=&quot;job-details__description-header text-color-secondary font-family-secondary&quot; data-bind=&quot;i18n: &#39;job-details.employer-description-title&#39;&quot;&gt;About Us&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;job-details__description-content basic-formatter&quot; data-bind=&quot;html: pageData().job.corporateDescription&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Fanatics is building a leading global digital sports platform. We ignite the passions of global sports fans and maximize the presence and reach for our hundreds of sports partners globally by offering products and services across Fanatics Commerce, Fanatics Collectibles, and Fanatics Betting &amp;amp; Gaming, allowing sports fans to Buy, Collect, and Bet. Through the Fanatics platform, sports fans can buy licensed fan gear, jerseys, lifestyle and streetwear products, headwear, and hardgoods; collect physical and digital trading cards, sports memorabilia, and other digital assets; and bet as the company builds its Sportsbook and iGaming platform. Fanatics has an established database of over 100 million global sports fans; a global partner network with approximately 900 sports properties, including major national and international professional sports leagues, players associations, teams, colleges, college conferences and retail partners, 2,500 athletes and celebrities, and 200 exclusive athletes; and over 2,000 retail locations, including its Lids retail stores. Our more than 22,000 employees are committed to relentlessly enhancing the fan experience and delighting sports fans globally.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Company&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fanatics Collectibles is a new company operating at the intersection of collectibles, culture, and technology. Backed by world-class investors, operators, and sports &amp;amp; entertainment partners, we are building the global leader in next-generation collectibles. As part of the broader Fanatics ecosystem, we leverage a digital sports platform that spans over 900 sports properties and engages more than 81 million fans. Together, we are reimagining every part of the collectibles experience for fans, partners, and creators.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Sr. Partner Quality Manager (3&lt;sup&gt;rd&lt;/sup&gt; party vendors) ensures that all Topps and Fanatics Collectibles products are manufactured to the highest standards of quality, integrity, and timeliness. This position focuses on print, finishing, and packout quality at external partners; interfaces with internal product development teams and the broader external supply chain; and reports directly to the Vice President of Quality Assurance and Compliance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This position is based in Sunrise, Florida, at a Fanatics external partner location and requires an on-site presence.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to work extended hours, including evenings, weekends, holidays, and overtime, based on production demands.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Trading card or collectibles manufacturing experience is highly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel up to 50% is required to support additional external partners, press approvals, pack outs, audits, and other production needs. Approved travel expenses will be reimbursed in accordance with company policy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience/Education:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor’s degree preferred&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years in quality assurance in commercial print and packaging&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years in a supervisory or management role&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Quality Assurance Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in developing and maintaining quality control systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to implement quality assurance and ensure compliance within set standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to work cross-functionally to define quality parameters and align SOPs, work instructions, training materials, and implementation plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience conducting quality process audits and addressing quality issues at external partner locations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Print Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extensive experience in commercial printing, coatings, and post-press embellishments, including cold foil, films, and embossing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expert knowledge of commercial print standards regarding color management in digital, conventional and UV printing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of managing quality operations and meeting production targets related to on-time delivery and adherence to quality standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing print and press approvals at external partner locations, including color, registration, stock, coatings, embellishments, and overall product appearance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience providing on-site quality oversight during packout operations to ensure finished products meet approved specifications, quality standards, and release requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Management Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Significant experience in a managerial or supervisory role within a busy manufacturing setting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience directly managing, developing, and holding a team accountable for performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to manage and optimize resources effectively&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Process Improvement Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated experience in process improvement and optimization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of implementing successful process improvement initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaboration and Cross-Functional Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working with cross-functional teams to achieve production goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to collaborate effectively with other departments, such as engineering, quality assurance, and supply chain.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing external partner relationships&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Essential Functions and Responsibilities:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Supervision and Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure external partners have clear direction regarding quality standards and parameters.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to troubleshoot production issues and implement effective solutions on-site at external partner locations, including issues involving prepress files, proofing, stock, and product specifications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong decision-making capabilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Innovative thinking to improve current production processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to lead and influence external partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent interpersonal communication skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conflict resolution and team-building abilities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong organizational and time management skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Quality Control:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attend product engineering and BOM (Bill of Materials) reviews, evaluate risks and inefficiencies, and communicate with the product development team to drive efficiency, meet quality standards, provide cost and time savings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to implement and monitor quality assurance programs&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Works cross-functionally to manage on-site and in-process quality assurance checks for all WIP and finished goods across the supply chain.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with the Fanatics Collectibles team to identify supply-chain challenges and develop and execute plans to address ongoing external partner issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborates with design, innovation, prepress, and scheduling to meet quality expectations regarding stock, color and the overall expected aesthetic of printed sheets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Implement and enforce quality audits, standards, procedures, and process controls at external partner locations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inspect and audit physical products to ensure they meet established quality specifications.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and resolve production and quality issues within the time frame required by the production schedule.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of applicable quality and commercial printing standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage and approve on-site print and press production at external partner locations, ensuring output meets approved proofs, specifications, color standards, and product requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide on-site oversight of partner packout operations, including verification of product configuration, packaging components, labeling, quantities, and finished-product quality.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Document approval decisions, communicate deviations, and escalate quality or production risks that could affect product integrity, schedule, or release dates.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Production Management:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Works with scheduling, project management, and engineering teams to ensure print and finishing processes are on schedule to support product release dates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate travel and on-site coverage based on partner production schedules, press approvals, packout activity, product launches, and identified quality risks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinates with other departments to ensure smooth workflow and efficient production&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Safety and Compliance:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure compliance with all regulatory and company standards for all printed work&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge of ISO standards and regulatory compliance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Continuous Improvement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and implement opportunities to improve production processes, efficiency, quality, and waste reduction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and coordinate cost-reduction and efficiency-improvement projects at external partner locations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and revise standard operating procedures and quality control processes in partnership with external partners and internal subject matter experts to improve efficiency and effectiveness.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reporting and Documentation:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain accurate and current records of production activities and initiatives, including output, quality performance, inventory levels, and program implementation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support KPI reporting and analysis related to quality, scrap, efficiency, equipment utilization, and headcount utilization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Collaboration and Communication:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inform the direct manager of any planned or unplanned absence from the assigned work schedule.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Facilitate effective communication between production teams and supporting departments, including engineering, quality assurance, finance, scheduling, logistics, security, and safety.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in cross-functional meetings to discuss and resolve production issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain open and constant communication about all department matters with the direct manager&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Performance Metrics:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track and analyze key performance indicators to measure production performance, support informed decisions, and drive continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide quarterly external partner scorecards covering capacity, communication, spend, on-time delivery, and quality defects.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Additional Skills:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in manufacturing software (e.g., ERP systems like SAP, Oracle).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficient in MS Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint, etc.)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to analyze and interpret production data to identify trends and areas for improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of process optimization and efficiency improvement&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Physical Demands&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prolonged periods of standing and walking throughout the manufacturing facility&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to lift and carry materials and equipment weighing up to 35 pounds.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Regular bending, stooping, and kneeling to monitor machinery, inspect WIP, and handle materials.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compliance with all safety protocols and regulations regarding PPE usage (including safety glasses, gloves, ear protection, etc.) as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to a manufacturing environment with varying temperatures, noise levels, and potential hazards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Tolerance for working in conditions that may include dust, fumes, and strong odors.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to remain alert and focused during long shifts and high-pressure situations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
