&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Supply Chain &amp;amp; Strategic Operations Associate&lt;/strong&gt; &lt;strong&gt;– Supply Planning Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location:&lt;/strong&gt; Sunnyvale, TX&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Reports to:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Supply Planning Director&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Language Requirement:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Fluent English&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;We are looking for a detail-oriented and proactive&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Supply Chain &amp;amp; Strategic Operations Associate&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;to join our Supply Planning team. The role will be responsible ensuring we have a robust operational execution plan to deliver our global upcoming program schedule. Will partner cross-functionally with Commercial, Brand, Project Management, and Operations to develop and implement strategies that align investment decisions with available operational capacity and levers. Additionally, this role will collaborate with Supply Chain leaders to support high-impact initiatives.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Capacity Model&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Serve as the primary owner for a defined portion of the capacity model (end-to-end demand vs capacity for card manufacturing process)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Ensure model accurately reflects the current business conditions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Identify and implement enhancements targeting model accuracy, scalability and/or coverage&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Quarterly Planning Review (QPR) Modelling &amp;amp; Insights&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Manage model refreshes in alignment with the QPR planning cadence&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Translate model outputs into actionable insights that highlight risks, constraints, and bottlenecks&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Develop data-driven recommendations to optimize capacity, mitigate risks, and align resources to forecasted demand&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Present finding and recommendations to inform leadership decision-making&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Partner cross-functionally to address action items identified during QPR&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Lead the development of high-level execution plans to resolve capacity gaps, resource constraints, and operational bottlenecks&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Support Supply Chain Initiatives&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Partner with Supply Chain leadership on high-impact projects requiring analytics, modelling, and/or project coordination&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Build and enhance forecasting and operational planning models&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Assist with new technology deployment and process implementation&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Support capital expenditure (CapEx) planning, equipment selection, and installation analysis&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;Develop and document Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs) to support scalable and repeatable operations&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We’re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;3–5 years of experience in Supply Chain, Operations, Planning, Finance, or Analytics&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Systems Knowledge:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Advanced Excel skills (modelling and scenario analysis); familiarity with BI tools (e.g., PowerBI) preferred&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Analytical Skills:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Experience building planning models, capacity planning, forecasting and/or operational performance analysis. Ability to translate data output into recommendations / insights. High attention to detail with a focus on accuracy and data integrity&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Strong written and verbal communication skills including ability to present to cross-functional leadership groups&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Mindset:&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;Detail-oriented, ownership mindset, proactive, comfortable in a fast-paced, high-growth environment and managing deadlines based on business needs&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;p1&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s1&quot; style=&quot;font-size: 12pt;&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;Ensure your Fanatics job offer is legitimate and don’t fall victim to fraud.&amp;nbsp; Fanatics never seeks payment from job applicants. Feel free to ask your recruiter for a phone call or other type of communication for interview, and ensure your communication is coming from a Fanatics email address (including @collectfanatics.com).&amp;nbsp; For added security, where possible, apply through our company website at&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.fanaticsinc.com/careers&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;s2&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;www.fanaticsinc.com/careers&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By submitting your application, you agree to our terms of service and acknowledge you have read our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://static1.squarespace.com/static/5ff494b9931735466ce28d5b/t/69de53bde2c02c25e9c38758/1776178110037/Candidate+Privacy+Policy+April+2026.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Candidate Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Fanatics will never ask candidates for money, banking information, or other sensitive personal information as part of the interview process. If you receive a suspicious message claiming to be from Fanatics recruiting, please do not respond and report it&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:recruiting-fraud@fanaticsinc.com&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;here&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 class=&quot;job-details__description-header text-color-secondary font-family-secondary&quot; data-bind=&quot;i18n: &#39;job-details.employer-description-title&#39;&quot;&gt;About Us&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;job-details__description-content basic-formatter&quot; data-bind=&quot;html: pageData().job.corporateDescription&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Fanatics is building a leading global digital sports platform. We ignite the passions of global sports fans and maximize the presence and reach for our hundreds of sports partners globally by offering products and services across Fanatics Commerce, Fanatics Collectibles, and Fanatics Betting &amp;amp; Gaming, allowing sports fans to Buy, Collect, and Bet. Through the Fanatics platform, sports fans can buy licensed fan gear, jerseys, lifestyle and streetwear products, headwear, and hardgoods; collect physical and digital trading cards, sports memorabilia, and other digital assets; and bet as the company builds its Sportsbook and iGaming platform. Fanatics has an established database of over 100 million global sports fans; a global partner network with approximately 900 sports properties, including major national and international professional sports leagues, players associations, teams, colleges, college conferences and retail partners, 2,500 athletes and celebrities, and 200 exclusive athletes; and over 2,000 retail locations, including its Lids retail stores. Our more than 22,000 employees are committed to relentlessly enhancing the fan experience and delighting sports fans globally.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fanatics Collectibles is a new company operating at the intersection of collectibles, culture, and technology. Backed by world-class investors, operators, and sports &amp;amp; entertainment partners, we are building the global leader in next-generation collectibles. As part of the broader Fanatics ecosystem, we leverage a digital sports platform that spans over 900 sports properties and engages more than 81 million fans. Together, we are reimagining every part of the collectibles experience for fans, partners, and creators.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fanatics Collectibles is seeking a recruiter in Japan at Fanatics Collectibles (Topps KK) supports the business by delivering high-quality, efficient recruitment across multiple functions in Japan. Reporting to the Director of International Recruiting, the role is responsible for full lifecycle recruitment, partnering closely with Hiring Managers to deliver strong hiring outcomes while contributing to continuous improvement efforts and consistently raising the hiring bar.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Core Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver end-to-end recruitment across multiple disciplines in Japan, managing roles from intake through offer and close&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with Hiring Managers to understand role requirements, team needs, and business context, providing practical guidance throughout the hiring process&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide sound counsel to Hiring Managers on hiring progress, candidate assessment, market conditions, and role alignment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Achieve quantitative recruitment goals, including agreed KPIs such as time to fill, hiring volume, pipeline health, and candidate experience measures&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure timely and accurate entry, analysis, and reporting of recruitment data, providing the Director and leadership with actionable insights on hiring progress, pipeline health, market trends, bottlenecks, and outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively identify and resolve recruitment bottlenecks, escalating risks and implementing solutions to maintain momentum&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to continuous improvement of recruitment processes, tools, and workflows to drive efficiency and consistency&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Actively utilize company-approved recruiting tools and technologies, including AI-enabled solutions, to improve recruiter productivity, candidate identification, sourcing effectiveness, and time to fill&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and execute proactive direct-sourcing strategies to identify, engage, and convert high-quality passive and active talent through LinkedIn, talent mapping, networking, referrals, databases, and other relevant channels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop talent maps and market intelligence for priority and hard-to-fill roles, using direct sourcing and external market insights to advise Hiring Managers and strengthen long-term pipelines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver a consistently positive and professional candidate experience across all stages of the recruitment lifecycle&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner effectively with Japan, regional, and global Human Resources colleagues and cross-functional stakeholders to ensure alignment and smooth hiring delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in ad hoc projects and initiatives as required, such as hiring campaigns, process improvements, tooling reviews, or broader Talent Acquisition and People projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain strong organization and prioritization in a fast-paced environment, balancing multiple roles and stakeholders effectively&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills and Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5–7 years of full lifecycle recruitment experience, with strong experience recruiting in Japan&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated knowledge of the Japan talent market and ability to recruit effectively in a Japanese business environment while operating within global recruitment processes and standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior corporate / in-house recruitment experience within a multinational corporation (MNC) is essential&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to manage multiple requisitions and stakeholders while meeting agreed KPIs and service levels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Professional fluency in both Japanese and English, with strong written and verbal communication skills and the ability to work effectively with stakeholders at varying levels of the organization&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience consulting with Hiring Managers and supporting hiring decisions in a dynamic environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong capability in recruitment data, analytics, and reporting, with experience translating hiring metrics and market insights into clear updates and recommendations for leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High tolerance for ambiguity and the ability to adapt to changing priorities, processes, and technology&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience using modern Applicant Tracking Systems, sourcing platforms, AI-enabled recruiting tools, and HR technologies; demonstrated comfort adopting new tools and technologies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Intermediate proficiency in Microsoft Office; database and reporting experience is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong interpersonal, organizational, and prioritization skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The above list of job duties is not exclusive or exhaustive and the post holder will be required to undertake such tasks as may reasonably be expected within the scope and grading of the post.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Subject to applicable laws, Fanatics Collectibles may choose to run a background check.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Ensure your Fanatics job offer is legitimate and don’t fall victim to fraud.&amp;nbsp; Fanatics never seeks payment from job applicants.&amp;nbsp;Feel free to ask your recruiter for a phone call or other type of communication for interview, and ensure your communication is coming from a Fanatics email address (including @collectfanatics.com).&amp;nbsp; For added security, where possible, apply through our company website at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.fanaticsinc.com/careers&quot;&gt;www.fanaticsinc.com/careers&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By submitting your application, you agree to our terms of service and acknowledge you have read our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://static1.squarespace.com/static/5ff494b9931735466ce28d5b/t/69de53bde2c02c25e9c38758/1776178110037/Candidate+Privacy+Policy+April+2026.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Candidate Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Fanatics will never ask candidates for money, banking information, or other sensitive personal information as part of the interview process. If you receive a suspicious message claiming to be from Fanatics recruiting, please do not respond and report it&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;mailto:recruiting-fraud@fanaticsinc.com&quot;&gt;&lt;em&gt;here&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;em&gt;.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h2 class=&quot;job-details__description-header text-color-secondary font-family-secondary&quot; data-bind=&quot;i18n: &#39;job-details.employer-description-title&#39;&quot;&gt;About Us&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;div class=&quot;job-details__description-content basic-formatter&quot; data-bind=&quot;html: pageData().job.corporateDescription&quot;&gt;
&lt;div&gt;Fanatics is building a leading global digital sports platform. We ignite the passions of global sports fans and maximize the presence and reach for our hundreds of sports partners globally by offering products and services across Fanatics Commerce, Fanatics Collectibles, and Fanatics Betting &amp;amp; Gaming, allowing sports fans to Buy, Collect, and Bet. Through the Fanatics platform, sports fans can buy licensed fan gear, jerseys, lifestyle and streetwear products, headwear, and hardgoods; collect physical and digital trading cards, sports memorabilia, and other digital assets; and bet as the company builds its Sportsbook and iGaming platform. Fanatics has an established database of over 100 million global sports fans; a global partner network with approximately 900 sports properties, including major national and international professional sports leagues, players associations, teams, colleges, college conferences and retail partners, 2,500 athletes and celebrities, and 200 exclusive athletes; and over 2,000 retail locations, including its Lids retail stores. Our more than 22,000 employees are committed to relentlessly enhancing the fan experience and delighting sports fans globally.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fanatics Collectibles is a new company operating at the intersection of collectibles, culture, and technology. Backed by world-class investors, operators, and sports &amp;amp; entertainment partners, we are building the global leader in next-generation collectibles. As part of the broader Fanatics ecosystem, we leverage a digital sports platform that spans over 900 sports properties and engages more than 81 million fans. Together, we are reimagining every part of the collectibles experience for fans, partners, and creators.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fanatics Collectibles is seeking a Trade Marketing Manager to help accelerate the growth of Topps trading card products in Japan. In this role, you will turn retail data into commercial action - using convenience store point-of-sale (POS) data as a core source of insight to shape how we plan, launch, distribute, and promote our products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Reporting to the Marketing Director (Japan) and working in close partnership with the Sales Director (Japan) and the broader Japan team, you will serve as a hub connecting Sales, Marketing, Product, retailers, and distributors/wholesalers - translating shopper and sales insights into practical strategies that improve sell-through, expand distribution, optimize trade investment, and strengthen partnerships. This role is equal parts analyst and operator, suited for someone who can move fluidly between reading the data and driving action on the shelf.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;POS Data &amp;amp; Consumer Insights&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the analysis of convenience store POS data, including sales by SKU, price point, promotional period, time of day, store, and region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate data into clear insights on shopper behavior, category trends, product performance, and commercial opportunities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build recurring reports and dashboards that provide stakeholders with a consistent view of sell-through, distribution, promotion performance, and emerging risks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Convert insights into actionable recommendations for product, pricing, promotion, assortment, distribution, messaging, and timing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Trade Strategy &amp;amp; Retail Execution&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop POS-backed trade marketing plans covering assortment, pricing, promotion, shelf space, and in-store execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Sales and retail customers to improve store-level execution, shopper conversion, and product sell-through.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plan and develop point-of-sale marketing materials - such as in-store visuals, video content, and POPs - that translate Sales and cross-functional needs into assets that drive sell-through at the shelf, partnering with marketing agencies from concept through delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the brand gatekeeper on the front lines of Sales - reviewing and providing guidance on sales assets developed by retail partners to ensure brand consistency and guideline compliance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build close working relationships with retailers and hobby shops - partnering with the Sales team to bring in-store events and activations to life where opportunities arise.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Partnership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the central connection point across Sales, Marketing, and Product, ensuring that plans are grounded in data and translated into coordinated execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work closely with retailers and distributors/wholesalers, using POS insights to support category management, demand forecasting, allocation, fill rate, and mutually beneficial growth plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product, Assortment &amp;amp; Distribution&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide Product teams with evidence-based input on product concepts, packaging, assortment, performance, and the future product roadmap for Japan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to place the right products in the right stores, expanding productive distribution while minimizing inventory risk.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Planning, Investment &amp;amp; Performance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support annual commercial and category planning by developing customer- and channel-specific growth strategies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate promotional and trade investments using data, recommending where to allocate resources to deliver stronger returns.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track key performance indicators, prepare post-activity reviews, and recommend actions that increase sell-through, distribution, and profitability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What We&#39;re Looking For&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years of experience in trade marketing, category management, sales planning, commercial strategy, or a related role - within FMCG, consumer products, retail, or another data-driven industry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience analyzing POS, sell-out, or retail scan data and converting findings into commercial recommendations and in-store actions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience working with major retailers and distributors/wholesalers - convenience store experience in Japan is strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience collaborating across Sales, Marketing, Product, and regional or global teams in a matrixed organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Skills &amp;amp; Attributes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills in both Japanese and English.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical capability, with advanced proficiency in Excel and experience using business intelligence, dashboard, or reporting tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Structured thinker who can move from complex data to a clear insight, recommendation, and execution plan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Commercially minded collaborator who can influence internal teams and build productive, win-win relationships with customers and partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on and able to thrive in ambiguity - not every process here has an established playbook, and we&#39;re looking for someone who can make judgment calls with incomplete information and find satisfaction in figuring things out along the way.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Genuine passion for sports and collectibles is a must - paired with strong curiosity about shoppers, retail execution, and what drives category growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;The above list of job duties is not exclusive or exhaustive and the post holder will be required to undertake such tasks as may reasonably be expected within the scope and grading of the post.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;Subject to applicable laws, Fanatics Collectibles may choose to run a background check.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Ensure your Fanatics job offer is legitimate and don’t fall victim to fraud.&amp;nbsp; Fanatics never seeks payment from job applicants.&amp;nbsp;Feel free to ask your recruiter for a phone call or other type of communication for interview, and ensure your communication is coming from a Fanatics email address (including @collectfanatics.com).&amp;nbsp; For added security, where possible, apply through our company website at&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;http://www.fanaticsinc.com/careers&quot;&gt;www.fanaticsinc.com/careers&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;
&lt;p&gt;By submitting your application, you agree to our terms of service and acknowledge you have read our&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://static1.squarespace.com/static/5ff494b9931735466ce28d5b/t/69de53bde2c02c25e9c38758/1776178110037/Candidate+Privacy+Policy+April+2026.pdf&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Candidate Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
